    <div id="vgn-funds-profile-cf-ele" data-vgn-funds-content-fragments='{&#34;fund_definitions_whats_an_asset_class&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_whats_an_asset_class&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_whats_an_asset_class&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;An asset class is a general category of investments. They&#39;re grouped by similarities in how they&#39;re traded and how they&#39;re regulated. Asset classes include:&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;ul&amp;gt;&amp;lt;li&amp;gt;Stocks (equity)&amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;&amp;lt;li&amp;gt;Fixed income (bonds)&amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;&amp;lt;li&amp;gt;Money market and cash equivalent&amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;&amp;lt;li&amp;gt;Balanced (multi-asset) These funds invest in both stocks and bonds.&amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;&amp;lt;li&amp;gt;Sector and specialty (provide access to specific industries, like energy, real estate, and health care)&amp;lt;/li&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/ul&amp;gt;&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_daily_market_value&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_daily_market_value&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_daily_market_value&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The net asset value of a money market fund&#39;s holdings based on the market prices of the fund&#39;s securities. This value is calculated out to 4 decimal places.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_risk_scale&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Risk is a measure of how likely it is that you could lose money in an investment. Knowing the risk level you&#39;re comfortable with and the length of time you expect to invest can help you select an appropriate fund for your investing needs.&lt;br>\n&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The potential for risk in Vanguard funds can be categorized in levels from 1 to 5. Knowing the risk level you&#39;re comfortable with and the length of time you expect to invest can help you select an appropriate fund for your investing needs.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_market_price_returns&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/price/fund_definitions_market_price_returns&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;Market price&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Effective July 15, 2024, the market price returns are calculated using the official closing price as reported by the ETF\u2019s primary exchange. Prior to July 15, 2024, the market price returns were calculated using the midpoint between the bid and ask prices as of the closing time of the New York Stock Exchange (typically 4 p.m., Eastern time). The returns shown do not represent the returns you would receive if you traded shares at other times.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_strategyfilter_totalmarketetf&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/configuration/configuration_strategyfilter_totalmarketetf&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_strategyfilter_totalmarketETF&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>[&#39;VTI&#39;, &#39;BND&#39;, &#39;VXUS&#39;, &#39;BNDX&#39;]&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_record_date&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_record_date&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_record_date&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The date used to determine who is eligible to receive a company&#39;s or fund&#39;s next distribution of dividends or capital gains.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_also_available_links_etf_and_lower_investors&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_also_available_links_etf_and_lower_investors&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_also_available_links_etf_and_lower_investors&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Also available as an &lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/etfs/profile/tickerETF\&#34;>ETF&lt;\/a> (starting at the price of one share) and at a lower minimum as an &lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/mutual-funds/profile/tickerInvestor\&#34;>Investor Shares&lt;\/a> mutual fund&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/mutual-funds/profile/tickerInvestor\&#34;>&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_etf_shares_redeemable&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_etf_shares_redeemable&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_etf_shares_redeemable&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>Vanguard ETFs as a share class:&lt;\/b> Vanguard ETFs® (exchange-traded funds) are a class of shares listed for trading on an exchange. The shares are available only through a broker, including Vanguard Brokerage Services®.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;i>Vanguard ETF® Shares are not redeemable with the issuing fund other than in very large aggregations worth millions of dollars. Instead, investors must buy and sell Vanguard ETF Shares in the secondary market and hold those shares in a brokerage account. In doing so, the investor may incur brokerage commissions and may pay more than net asset value when buying and receive less than net asset value when selling.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Total returns:&lt;\/b> Short-term total return information is provided only as a service. Historical performance\u2014particularly short-term performance\u2014is no guarantee of future returns. Price, yield, and return on an actual investment will fluctuate, and you may have a gain or loss when you sell. Average annual returns include changes in price and reinvestments of dividends and capital gains. Since-inception returns for less than 1 year and year-to-date returns aren&#39;t annualized. Index performance is provided as a benchmark but isn&#39;t illustrative of any particular investment. You can&#39;t invest in an index.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Standardized returns:&lt;\/b> To see quarterly fee-adjusted returns, refer to the &lt;b>Price &amp;amp; Performance&lt;\/b> details.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Expense ratios:&lt;\/b> Expense ratios are displayed on &lt;b>Overview&lt;\/b>. For investments that are less than 1 fiscal year old, expense ratios are estimated.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Risk:&lt;\/b> All investing is subject to risk, including the possible loss of the money you invest. Funds that concentrate on a relatively narrow market sector face the risk of higher share-price volatility. Investments in stocks or bonds issued by non-U.S. companies are subject to risks including country/regional risk and currency risk.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_non_vanguard_brokerage_redem_fee&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_non_vanguard_brokerage_redem_fee&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_non_vanguard_brokerage_redem_fee&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>$50 early redemption fee will apply to all sales within 60 calendar days of the most recent purchase trade date.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;gnma-fund&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/gnma_fund_definition/gnma-fund&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Investors should be cautious in evaluating Vanguard GNMA Fund&#39;s current SEC yield. This yield, while accurate, could decline significantly because of mortgage refinancing due to lower interest rates. This could reduce future income from the fund, since it invests in mortgage-backed securities.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_historical_price_money_market&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/price/fund_definitions_historical_price_money_market&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_historical_price_money_market&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Price history does not apply to money market funds because they historically have maintained a stable price of $1 per share. However, you can conduct a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a>&lt;\/a>&lt;a href=\&#34;%7B%7Burl%7D%7Dfunds/tools/pricehistorysearch\&#34;>Price History Search&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;to review historical yield information, which may be useful when evaluating money market funds.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_compound_yield&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_compound_yield&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_compound_yield&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Compound yield is the interest earned on the original principal invested and also on the interest earned in previous periods.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_bfp_toggles&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/configuration/configuration_bfp_toggles&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_bfp_toggles&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>{&lt;br>\n&amp;quot;classification&amp;quot;:true,&lt;br>\n&amp;quot;diversification&amp;quot;:false,&lt;br>\n&amp;quot;allocation&amp;quot;:false,&lt;br>\n&amp;quot;characteristics&amp;quot;:false&lt;br>\n}&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_market_price&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/footnote_market_price&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;footnote_market_price&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Effective July 15, 2024, the market price returns are calculated using the official closing price as reported by the ETF\u2019s primary exchange. Prior to July 15, 2024, the market price returns were calculated using the midpoint between the bid and ask prices as of the closing time of the New York Stock Exchange (typically 4 p.m., Eastern time). The returns shown do not represent the returns you would receive if you traded shares at other times.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_fair_value_pricing_information&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_fair_value_pricing_information&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_fair_value_pricing_information&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>An index fund\u2019s return may sometimes appear to diverge from the return of its benchmark index a bit more than would be expected. This may be the result of a fair-value pricing adjustment.&lt;br>\n&lt;br>\n&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>These adjustments, which are required by the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, address pricing discrepancies that may arise because of time-zone differences among global securities markets. Foreign securities may trade on exchanges that close many hours before a fund\u2019s closing share price is calculated in the United States, generally at 4 p.m., Eastern time. In the hours between the close of the foreign market and the close of the U.S. market, the value of these foreign securities may change\u2014for example, because of company-specific announcements or market-wide developments. Such price changes are not immediately reflected in international index values.&lt;br>\n&lt;br>\n&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Fair-value pricing takes such changes into account in calculating the fund\u2019s daily net asset value (NAV) to help ensure that the NAV doesn\u2019t include stale prices. The result can be a temporary divergence between the return of the fund and that of its benchmark index\u2014a difference that usually corrects itself when the foreign markets reopen.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_yield_-to_-maturity&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_yield_-to_-maturity&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_yield_to_maturity&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The rate of return an investor would receive if a security is held to its maturity date.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_ntf&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_ntf&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_NTF&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A no-transaction-fee (NTF) fund is exactly that\u2014a fund that charges no fees when it&#39;s bought or sold. Vanguard Brokerage, however, imposes an NTF redemption fee on shares held less than a specified period. For more information, see the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investing/transaction-fees-commissions/etfs\&#34; title=\&#34;Follow link\&#34;>Vanguard Brokerage Services® commission and fee schedules&lt;\/a>.&lt;br>\n&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The NTF redemption fee is in addition to any short-term redemption fees charged by the fund family. View a fund&#39;s prospectus for information on redemption fees.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_expense_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Expressed as a percentage, the expense ratios are fees charged to investors to cover a fund or ETF&#39;s operating costs. They&#39;re deducted from dividend and capital gains distributions, not the principal.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_performance_data_for_periods&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_performance_data_for_periods&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_performance_data_for_periods&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Performance data for periods of less than one year does not reflect the deduction of purchase and redemption fees that may apply. All other performance data are adjusted for purchase and redemption fees, where applicable. If this fee was included, the performance would be lower.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_non_vg_fund_trasfer_only&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_non_vg_fund_trasfer_only&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_non_vg_fund_trasfer_only&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>This fund can be transferred to your Vanguard brokerage account but isn&#39;t available for purchase through FundAccess®.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_announcements&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_announcements&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_announcements&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>0301---The Vanguard Mid-Cap Growth Fund changed investment managers on November 17, 2025. This may result in capital gains distributions, which could be taxable if you hold shares in a regular (taxable) account. Vanguard provides monthly updates on estimated realized and unrealized gains in the &amp;quot;Distributions&amp;quot; section of the fund\u2019s website page.|0967--- On March 24, 2026, Vanguard announced that the ETF will complete a 6:1 share split effective April&amp;nbsp; 21, 2026. The share split results in a decrease of the price per share of the ETF with a proportionate increase in the number of shares outstanding. Historical share price data will not be adjusted for the split. Although certain data may reflect both pre- and post-split prices, returns are not impacted.|3138---&lt;b>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/b>On March 24, 2026, Vanguard announced that the ETF will complete a 5:1 share split effective April&amp;nbsp; 21, 2026. The share split results in a decrease of the price per share of the ETF with a proportionate increase in the number of shares outstanding. Historical share price data will not be adjusted for the split. Although certain data may reflect both pre- and post-split prices, returns are not impacted.|3341---On March 24, 2026, Vanguard announced that the ETF will complete a 6:1 share split effective April&amp;nbsp; 21, 2026. The share split results in a decrease of the price per share of the ETF with a proportionate increase in the number of shares outstanding. Historical share price data will not be adjusted for the split. Although certain data may reflect both pre- and post-split prices, returns are not impacted.|0939---On March 24, 2026, Vanguard announced that the ETF will complete a 4:1 share split effective April&amp;nbsp; 21, 2026. The share split results in a decrease of the price per share of the ETF with a proportionate increase in the number of shares outstanding. Historical share price data will not be adjusted for the split. Although certain data may reflect both pre- and post-split prices, returns are not impacted.|0958---On March 24, 2026, Vanguard announced that the ETF will complete a 8:1 share split effective April&amp;nbsp; 21, 2026. The share split results in a decrease of the price per share of the ETF with a proportionate increase in the number of shares outstanding. Historical share price data will not be adjusted for the split. Although certain data may reflect both pre- and post-split prices, returns are not impacted.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_return_on_equity&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_return_on_equity&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_return_on_equity&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The amount, expressed as a percentage, earned on a company&#39;s common stock investment for a specific time frame. This figure tells shareholders how effectively their money is being utilized.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_total_market_etf&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_total_market_etf&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_total_market_etf&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Total market ETFs employ an indexing investment approach designed to track the performance of broad indexes representing the bond or stock markets.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_non_vanguard_mf_investing_prospectus&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_non_vanguard_mf_investing_prospectus&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>The fund profiles are intended to provide a brief summary of the mutual funds. Not all disclosures apply to all funds. Cost data shown here may be incomplete. Please refer to the fund&#39;s prospectus for full information on advisory fees, distribution charges, and other expenses. You should read the prospectus before investing in any fund to ensure the fund is appropriate for your goals and risk tolerance.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vgcix&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vgcix&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vgcix&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Investors should be mindful in evaluating the Vanguard Global Credit Bond Fund Investor Shares current SEC yield. This yield, while accurately calculated based on the SEC requirements, does not capture returns resulting from currency hedging. This fund includes bonds that are denominated in local currencies and hedges nearly all returns back to the U.S. dollar to minimize currency risk. Currency hedging can have a meaningful impact on total returns over the short term.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_realized_and_unrealized-gains_-losses_understand_the_tax-implications&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_realized_and_unrealized-gains_-losses_understand_the_tax-implications&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_realized_and_unrealized_gains_losses_understand_the_tax_implications&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;A fund&#39;s realized and unrealized capital gains and losses can provide helpful information about the tax implications of holding a particular fund in a taxable account. This is true of both realized and unrealized capital gains and losses.\n\n(These tax implications don&#39;t apply to investors holding a fund in a tax-deferred account, such as an IRA or employer-sponsored retirement plan.)&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_esg&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_esg&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_ESG&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Sometimes referred to as \u201csocially responsible investing (SRI)\u201d and \u201csustainable investing\u201d, ESG investing offers a way for you to invest in funds that consider environmental, social, and governance issues.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_pe_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_pe_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_pe_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The price per share of a stock divided by its per-share earnings over the past year. For a portfolio, the ratio is the weighted average price/earnings ratio of the stocks it holds.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_vanguard_advisor_services&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_vanguard_advisor_services&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_vanguard_advisor_services&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>Vanguard Advice Select Dividend Growth fund is available exclusively to clients of&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/campaign/active-investing\&#34;>Vanguard Personal Advisor Services&lt;\/a>.&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_acquired_fund_fees_and_expenses&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/footnote_acquired_fund_fees_and_expenses&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;footnote_acquired_fund_fees_and_expenses&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The acquired fund fees and expenses based on the fees and expenses of the underlying funds.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_equity_index&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_equity_index&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_equity_index&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>\u2022 Seeks to collect the carry differential between high-carry and low-carry countries.&lt;br>\n\u2022 Holds long positions in higher yielding equity index futures, while shorting lower yielding equity index futures.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_maturity&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_maturity&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_maturity&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>This is the date that the issuer of a money market instrument or bond agrees to repay the principal\u2014or face value\u2014to the buyer. For a fund, it&#39;s calculated by taking an average of the maturities for all of the bonds that the fund invests in.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_current_day_market_price&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/price/fund_definitions_current_day_market_price&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;Market price&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The price at which the security last traded in the secondary market. Please be aware that price data may be subject to at least a 15-minute delay on vanguard.com relative to primary exchanges.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vmsxx&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vmsxx&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vmsxx&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Price history does not apply to money market funds because they historically have maintained a stable price of $1 per share.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_distribution_by_effective_maturity&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_distribution_by_effective_maturity&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_distribution_by_effective_maturity&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Represents the percentage of fund assets in each maturity category. Effective Maturity methodology is used to determine the maturity category each holding is allocated to. Effective Maturity is defined as the length of time until a fixed income security held by a fund reaches maturity and is repaid, taking into consideration that an action such as a call or refunding may cause some bonds to be repaid before they mature.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_market_price&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_market_price&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_market_price&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The Market price is determined by the midpoint between the bid and asked prices as of the closing time of the New York Stock Exchange (typically 4 p.m., Eastern time) on business days.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_balanced_risk_strategies&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_balanced_risk_strategies&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_balanced_risk_strategies&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Although the fund generally expects to maintain an approximate equal weighting among the strategies, the advisor may increase or decrease a strategy&#39;s weighting within the fund to a level deemed appropriate to further the fund&#39;s investment objective. In addition, the advisor may discontinue use of any of the strategies or add one or more new strategies if deemed to be in the best interests of the fund.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_also_available_links_lower_etf&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_also_available_links_lower_etf&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_also_available_links_lower_etf&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Also available at a lower cost as an &lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/etfs/profile/ticker\&#34;>ETF&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_before_investing_in_529&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_before_investing_in_529&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_before_investing_in_529&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>Please note: Before investing in any 529 plan, you should consider whether your or the beneficiary&#39;s home state offers a 529 plan that provides its taxpayers with favorable state tax and other benefits that are only available through investment in the home state&#39;s 529 plan. Other state benefits may include financial aid, scholarship funds, and protection from creditors. You also should consult your financial, tax, or other advisor to learn more about how state-based benefits (or any limitations) would apply to your specific circumstances. You also may wish to contact directly your home state&#39;s 529 plan(s), or any other 529 plan, to learn more about those plan features, benefits, and limitations. Keep in mind that state-based benefits should be one of many appropriately weighted factors to be considered when making an investment decision.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_mf_performance_prospectuses&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_mf_performance_prospectuses&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_mf_performance_prospectuses&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>Before you invest, consider the fund\u2019s objective, risks, charges, and expenses. The fund\u2019s prospectus (or summary prospectus, if available) will tell you these important facts and more. Read it carefully.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vtapx&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vtapx&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vtapx&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The yield quoted is the real yield, or the yield before adjusting for inflation. The actual yield on Vanguard Short-Term Inflation-Protected Securities Fund will be a combination of the real yield and an inflation adjustment. A complete estimate of the funds yield requires that an estimate of future inflation be added to the real yield. Because inflation fluctuates, it cannot be projected into the future precisely enough to be included in the yield quote. The inflation adjustment is based on changes to the Consumer Price Index (CPI) and can either be positive or negative, based on the change to the CPI. Investors interested in maintaining the purchasing power of their investment should reinvest their dividend distributions.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_strategyfilter_all_in_one&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/configuration/configuration_strategyfilter_all_in_one&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_strategyfilter_all_in_one&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>[&#39;0914&#39;, &#39;0723&#39;, &#39;0122&#39;, &#39;0724&#39;, &#39;0308&#39;, &#39;0682&#39;, &#39;0304&#39;, &#39;0695&#39;, &#39;0305&#39;, &#39;0696&#39;, &#39;0306&#39;, &#39;0699&#39;,&#39;1487&#39;, &#39;1691&#39;, &#39;1791&#39;, &#39;V009&#39;]&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_vanguard_brokerage_services&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_vanguard_brokerage_services&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_vanguard_brokerage_services&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>You must buy and sell Vanguard ETF Shares through Vanguard Brokerage Services (we offer them commission-free) or through another broker (which may charge commissions). See the&amp;nbsp;&lt;u>&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/client-benefits/investment-fees\&#34;>Vanguard Brokerage Services commission and fee schedules&lt;\/a>&lt;\/u>&amp;nbsp;for full details. Vanguard ETF Shares are not redeemable directly with the issuing fund other than in very large aggregations worth millions of dollars. ETFs are subject to market volatility. When buying or selling an ETF, you will pay or receive the current market price, which may be more or less than net asset value.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_non_vanguard_etf_expense_ratios&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_non_vanguard_etf_expense_ratios&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_non_vanguard_etf_expense_ratios&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Non-Vanguard ETF expense ratio data provided by Morningstar are for the fund&#39;s latest fiscal year and may vary from current expense ratios. Such data do not reflect fee waivers, expense recoupments, or expense reimbursements, which the applicable fund manager may discontinue at any time. For more complete information about fees and expenses, see the fee table in the fund&#39;s prospectus. Vanguard is not responsible for the accuracy or timeliness of third-party data.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_529_expense_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_529_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_529_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Fees charged to investors to cover operating costs, expressed as a percentage. The money is deducted from investment returns before they&#39;re given to investors. For example, if you had $10,000 invested in a portfolio with an expense ratio of 0.20%, you&#39;d pay about $20 a year out of your investment returns.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_share_split_funds&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/configuration/configuration_share_split_funds&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_share_split_funds&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>[ { ticker: VUG, splitDate: 04/21/2026, price: 81.49 }, { ticker: MGK, splitDate: 04/21/2026, price: 82.35 }, { ticker: VOOG, splitDate: 04/21/2026, price: 76.23 }, { ticker: VO, splitDate: 04/21/2026, price: 76.61 }, { ticker: VGT, splitDate: 04/21/2026, price: 100.97 }, { ticker: IVOO, splitDate: 03/14/2023, price: 82.86 }, { ticker: IVOV, splitDate: 03/14/2023, price: 76.96 }, { ticker: IVOG, splitDate: 03/14/2023, price: 86.24 }, { ticker: VIOO, splitDate: 03/14/2023, price: 87.73 }, { ticker: VIOV, splitDate: 03/14/2023, price: 80.27 }, { ticker: VIOG, splitDate: 03/14/2023, price: 93.47 }, { ticker: VONV, splitDate: 04/20/2021, price: 67.91 }, { ticker: VTWO, splitDate: 04/20/2021, price: 87.63 }, { ticker: VONG, splitDate: 04/20/2021, price: 66.28 }, { ticker: VOO, splitDate: 10/24/2013, price: 160.46 }, { ticker: VTI, splitDate: 06/18/2008, price: 67.50 }, { ticker: VWO, splitDate: 06/18/2008, price: 49.07 } ]&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vipsx&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vipsx&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vipsx&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The yield quoted is the real yield, or the yield before adjusting for inflation. The actual yield on Vanguard Inflation-Protected Securities Fund will be a combination of the real yield and an inflation adjustment. A complete estimate of the funds yield requires that an estimate of future inflation be added to the real yield. Because inflation fluctuates, it cannot be projected into the future precisely enough to be included in the yield quote. The inflation adjustment is based on changes to the Consumer Price Index (CPI) and can either be positive or negative, based on the change to the CPI. Investors interested in maintaining the purchasing power of their investment should reinvest their dividend distributions.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_vanguard_investment_manager&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_vanguard_investment_manager&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_vanguard_investment_manager&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan is a Nevada Trust administered by the office of the Nevada State Treasurer&lt;br>\n &lt;\/b>The Vanguard Group, Inc., serves as the Investment Manager for The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan and through its affiliate, Vanguard Marketing Corporation, markets and distributes the Plan. Ascensus Broker Dealer Services, LLC, serves as Program Manager and has overall responsibility for the day-to-day operations. The Plan&#39;s portfolios, although they invest in Vanguard mutual funds, are not mutual funds. Investment returns are not guaranteed, and you could lose money by investing in the Plan.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_non_vg_expense_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_non_vg_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_non_vg_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Non-Vanguard fund expense ratio data provided by Morningstar are for the fund&#39;s latest fiscal year and may vary from current expense ratios. Such data do not reflect fee waivers, expense recoupments, or expense reimbursements, which the applicable fund manager may discontinue at any time. For more complete information about fees and expenses, see the fee table in the fund&#39;s prospectus. Vanguard is not responsible for the accuracy or timeliness of third-party data.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_past_performance&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_past_performance&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_past_performance&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>The performance data shown represent past performance, which is not a guarantee of future results. Investment returns and principal value will fluctuate, so that investors&#39; shares, when sold, may be worth more or less than their original cost. Current performance may be lower or higher than the performance data cited.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_also_available_links_etf&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_also_available_links_etf&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_also_available_links_etf&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Also available as an&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/etfs/profile/ticker\&#34;>ETF&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;(starting at the price of $1).&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_equities&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_equities&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_equities&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>\u2022 Seeks to capture the higher risk-adjusted performance of low-volatility stocks.&lt;br>\n\u2022 Holds long positions in low-volatility stocks, while taking short positions in high volatility-stocks.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_money_market_cusip_terms_and_conditions&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_money_market_cusip_terms_and_conditions&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_money_market_cusip_terms_and_conditions&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The Fund&#39;s holdings contain CUSIP numbers, which are subject to certain terms and conditions. In order to access the holdings&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://retaemsitesauth.rett.c1.vanguard.com/editor.html/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/Visitor%20legal%20terms%20Please%20read%20and%20indicate%20your%20acceptance%20of%20these%20Additional%20Terms%20by%20clicking%20on%20the%20link%20at%20the%20bottom%20of%20the%20page.%20You%20are%20about%20to%20enter%20into%20an%20Agreement%20with%20CUSIP%20Global%20Services.%20If%20you%20do%20not%20agree%20with%20these%20terms,%20then%20please%20do%20not%20click%20%22I%20Accept.,%22.%20By%20clicking%20%22I%20Accept.,%22,%20you%20agree%20to%20accept%20and%20be%20bound%20by%20the%20terms%20and%20conditions%20of%20this%20Agreement.%20%20The%20CUSIP%20Data%20contained%20in%20vanguard.com,%20personal.vanguard.com,%20advisors.vanguard.com,%20and%20institutional.vanguard.com%20(the%20%22Vanguard%20Web%20Site%22)%20consists%20of%20security%20identifiers%20and%20related%20descriptive%20information%20(%22the%20CUSIP%20Database%22)%20and%20is%20protected%20under%20the%20U.S.%20copyright%20laws%20and%20is%20licensed%20with%20permission%20from%20CUSIP%20Global%20Services%20(%22CGS%22),%20on%20behalf%20of%20the%20American%20Bankers%20Association%20%22ABA%22.%20%20Visitor%20agrees%20and%20acknowledges%20that%20the%20CUSIP%20Database%20and%20the%20information%20contained%20therein%20is%20and%20shall%20remain%20valuable%20intellectual%20property%20owned%20by,%20or%20licensed%20to,%20CUSIP%20Global%20Services%20and%20the%20American%20Bankers%20Association%20(%22ABA%22),%20and%20that%20no%20proprietary%20rights%20are%20being%20transferred%20to%20visitor%20in%20such%20materials%20or%20in%20any%20of%20the%20information%20contained%20therein.%20Any%20use%20of%20the%20CUSIP%20Data%20by%20visitor%20outside%20of%20the%20clearing%20and%20settlement%20of%20transactions%20requires%20a%20license%20from%20CGS,%20along%20with%20an%20associated%20fee%20based%20on%20usage.%20Visitor%20agrees%20that%20misappropriation%20or%20misuse%20of%20such%20materials%20will%20cause%20serious%20damage%20to%20CGS%20and%20ABA,%20and%20that%20in%20such%20event%20money%20damages%20may%20not%20constitute%20sufficient%20compensation%20to%20CGS%20and%20ABA;%20consequently,%20visitor%20agrees%20that%20in%20the%20event%20of%20any%20misappropriation%20or%20misuse,%20CGS%20and%20ABA%20shall%20have%20the%20right%20to%20obtain%20injunctive%20relief%20in%20addition%20to%20any%20other%20legal%20or%20financial%20remedies%20to%20which%20CGS%20and%20ABA%20may%20be%20entitled.%20%20Visitor%20agrees%20that%20it%20shall%20not%20publish%20nor%20distribute%20in%20any%20medium%20the%20CUSIP%20Database%20or%20any%20substantial%20portion%20of%20the%20information%20contained%20therein%20or%20summaries%20or%20subsets%20thereof%20to%20any%20person%20or%20entity.%20Visitor%20may%20not%20create%20or%20maintain%20a%20master%20file%20or%20database%20of%20CUSIP%20identifiers%20or%20descriptions%20for%20itself%20or%20any%20third%20party%20recipient%20that%20is%20intended%20to%20serve%20as%20a%20substitute%20for%20any%20CUSIP%20service.%20%20Visitor%20agrees%20not%20to:%20%20Violate%20the%20restrictions%20in%20any%20robot%20inclusion%20headers%20on%20the%20Vanguard%20Web%20Site%20or%20in%20any%20way%20bypass%20or%20circumvent%20any%20other%20measure%20employed%20to%20limit%20or%20prevent%20access%20to%20the%20CUSIP%20Data%20on%20the%20Vanguard%20Web%20Site;%20Violate%20the%20security%20of%20the%20Vanguard%20Web%20Site%20or%20attempt%20to%20gain%20unauthorized%20access%20to%20the%20Web%20Site,%20CUSIP%20Data,%20materials,%20information,%20computer%20systems%20or%20networks%20connected%20to%20Vanguard%20server,%20through%20hacking,%20password%20mining%20or%20any%20other%20means;%20or%20Interfere%20or%20attempt%20to%20interfere%20with%20the%20proper%20working%20of%20the%20Vanguard%20Web%20Site%20or%20any%20activities%20conducted%20on%20or%20through%20the%20Vanguard%20Web%20Site.%20NEITHER%20CGS,%20ABA%20NOR%20ANY%20OF%20THEIR%20AFFILIATES%20MAKE%20ANY%20WARRANTIES,%20EXPRESS%20OR%20IMPLIED,%20AS%20TO%20THE%20ACCURACY,%20ADEQUACY%20OR%20COMPLETENESS%20OF%20ANY%20OF%20THE%20INFORMATION%20CONTAINED%20IN%20THE%20CUSIP%20DATABASE.%20ALL%20SUCH%20MATERIALS%20ARE%20PROVIDED%20TO%20VISITOR%20ON%20AN%20%22AS%20IS%22%20BASIS,%20WITHOUT%20ANY%20WARRANTIES%20AS%20TO%20MERCHANTABILITY%20OR%20FITNESS%20FOR%20A%20PARTICULAR%20PURPOSE%20OR%20USE%20NOR%20WITH%20RESPECT%20TO%20THE%20RESULTS%20WHICH%20MAY%20BE%20OBTAINED%20FROM%20THE%20USE%20OF%20SUCH%20MATERIALS.%20NEITHER%20CGS,%20ABA%20NOR%20THEIR%20AFFILIATES%20SHALL%20HAVE%20ANY%20RESPONSIBILITY%20OR%20LIABILITY%20FOR%20ANY%20ERRORS%20OR%20OMISSIONS%20NOR%20SHALL%20THEY%20BE%20LIABLE%20FOR%20ANY%20DAMAGES,%20WHETHER%20DIRECT%20OR%20INDIRECT,%20SPECIAL%20OR%20CONSEQUENTIAL,%20EVEN%20IF%20THEY%20HAVE%20BEEN%20ADVISED%20OF%20THE%20POSSIBILITY%20OF%20SUCH%20DAMAGES.%20IN%20NO%20EVENT%20SHALL%20THE%20LIABILITY%20OF%20CGS,%20ABA%20OR%20ANY%20OF%20THEIR%20AFFILIATES%20PURSUANT%20TO%20ANY%20CAUSE%20OF%20ACTION,%20WHETHER%20IN%20CONTRACT,%20TORT,%20OR%20OTHERWISE,%20EXCEED%20THE%20FEE%20PAID%20BY%20VISITOR%20FOR%20ACCESS%20TO%20SUCH%20MATERIALS%20IN%20THE%20MONTH%20IN%20WHICH%20SUCH%20CAUSE%20OF%20ACTION%20IS%20ALLEGED%20TO%20HAVE%20ARISEN.%20FURTHERMORE,%20CGS%20AND%20ABA%20SHALL%20HAVE%20NO%20RESPONSIBILITY%20OR%20LIABILITY%20FOR%20DELAYS%20OR%20FAILURES%20DUE%20TO%20CIRCUMSTANCES%20BEYOND%20THEIR%20CONTROL.%20%20Visitor%20agrees%20that%20the%20foregoing%20terms%20and%20conditions%20shall%20survive%20any%20termination%20of%20its%20right%20of%20access%20to%20the%20materials%20identified%20above.\&#34;>&lt;\/a>&lt;a>&lt;\/a>&lt;a href=\&#34;https://retaemsitesauth.rett.c1.vanguard.com/editor.html/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_money_market_cusip_terms_and_conditions#\&#34;>read and accept&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;these terms&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>and conditions.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_daily_liquid_assets&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_daily_liquid_assets&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_daily_liquid_assets&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Daily liquid assets generally consist of government securities, cash, and assets that will mature within 1 business day.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_for_more_information&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_for_more_information&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_for_more_information&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>For more information about Vanguard funds, visit vanguard.com to obtain a prospectus or, if available, a summary prospectus. Investment objectives, risks, charges, expenses, and other important information about a fund are contained in the prospectus; read and consider it carefully before investing.&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_cash&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_cash&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_cash&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A low-risk option for your short-term savings.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_hidden_fund_ids&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/configuration/configuration_hidden_fund_ids&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_hidden_fund_ids&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>0082,0082,0472,0465,0002,0006,0009,0040,0048,0072,0079,0084,0085,0098,0113,0123,0132,0307,0314,0533,0832,0835,0859,0860,0861,1231,1397,1967,0882,0872,0873,0096,0038,0115,0013,0070,0047,3640,0778,0018,0302,0124,0328,0526,0026,1662,1674,1651,1472,1462,0681,5101,0136,1862,5227,0227,0885,0544,1499,1497,0518,0018,0578,0078,1650,1482,1481,0302,0337,0234,0050,0558,0058,0299,0381,0398,0300,0019,0020,0012,0025,0131,0054,0055,0037,0074,1967,0025,0025,4524,4523,4543,4543&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_strategyfilters_cash&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/configuration_strategyfilters_cash&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_strategyfilters_cash&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>[&#39;VCTXX&#39;,&#39;VMRXX&#39;,&#39;VMSXX&#39;,&#39;VYFXX&#39;,&#39;VUSXX&#39;]&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_distribution_by_state_maturity&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_distribution_by_state_maturity&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_distribution_by_state_maturity&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Represents the percentage of fund assets in each maturity category. Stated Maturity methodology is used to determine the maturity category each holding is allocated to. Stated Maturity is defined as the stated maturity date for each fixed income security held by the fund.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_non_vanguard_mutual_fund_expense_ratios&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_non_vanguard_mutual_fund_expense_ratios&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Non-Vanguard fund expense ratio data provided by Morningstar are for the fund&#39;s latest fiscal year and may vary from current expense ratios. Such data do not reflect fee waivers, expense recoupments, or expense reimbursements, which the applicable fund manager may discontinue at any time. For more complete information about fees and expenses, see the fee table in the fund&#39;s prospectus. Vanguard is not responsible for the accuracy or timeliness of third-party data.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_etf_expense_ratios&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_etf_expense_ratios&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The &lt;a href=\&#34;#modal-fund_definitions_expense_ratio\&#34;>expense ratios&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;of exchange-traded funds (ETFs)&amp;nbsp;often are lower than corresponding mutual funds because ETFs are traded through brokerage firms, alleviating administrative costs. When purchasing or selling ETFs, however, you may incur&amp;nbsp;transaction costs that&amp;nbsp;would not apply to&amp;nbsp;no-load mutual funds.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_delayedprice&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_delayedprice&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_delayedprice&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Quotes delayed at least 15 minutes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;i>Source:&lt;\/i>&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=\&#34;primary-reinforce\&#34; href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/external-site-message?url=http://www.factset.com/\&#34; title=\&#34;Follow link\&#34;>FactSet&lt;\/a>&lt;i>.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_mf_taxable_money_market_lose_money&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_mf_taxable_money_market_lose_money&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_mf_taxable_money_market_lose_money&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard Cash Reserves Federal Money Market Fund and Vanguard Federal Money Market Fund:&amp;nbsp;&lt;i>You could lose money by investing in the Fund. Although the Fund seeks to preserve the value of your investment at $1.00 per share, it cannot guarantee it will do so. An investment in the Fund is not a bank account and is not insured or guaranteed by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or any other government agency. The Fund\u2019s sponsor is not required to reimburse the Fund for losses, and you should not expect that the sponsor will provide financial support to the Fund at any time, including during periods of market stress.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_final_maturity_date&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_final_maturity_date&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_final_maturity_date&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The final legal maturity date taking into account any maturity date extensions that may be put into effect at the issuer&#39;s option.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_redemption_gate&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_redemption_gate&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_redemption_gate&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A redemption gate is in effect. Shares of the fund cannot be redeemed at this time.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_weekly_liquid_assets&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_weekly_liquid_assets&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_weekly_liquid_assets&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Weekly liquid assets generally consist of government securities, cash, and assets that will mature within 5 business days.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_ex_dividend_date&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_ex_dividend_date&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_ex_dividend_date&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The date when a distribution of dividends and/or capital gains is deducted from the share price of a mutual fund or stock. On the ex-dividend date, the share price drops by the amount of the distribution (plus or minus any market activity).&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_r_squared&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_r_squared&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_r_squared&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A measure of how much of a portfolio&#39;s performance can be explained by the returns from the overall market (or a benchmark index). If a portfolio&#39;s total return precisely matched that of the overall market or benchmark, its R-squared would be 1.00. If a portfolio&#39;s return bore no relationship to the returns of the market or benchmark, its R-squared would be 0. At Vanguard, R-squared is based on returns over the past 36 months for both the fund and the index.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_no_transaction_fee&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/footnote_no_transaction_fee&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;footnote_no_transaction_fee&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>No-transaction-fee (NTF) funds may carry a redemption fee. See the &lt;a class=\&#34;primary-reinforce\&#34; href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/client-benefits/investment-fees\&#34;>Vanguard brokerage commission and fee schedule&lt;\/a> for more information.&lt;a title=\&#34;Vanguard brokerage commission and fee schedule\&#34; href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/client-benefits/investment-fees\&#34;>&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_also_available_links_admiral&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_also_available_links_admiral&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_also_available_links_admiral&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Also available as an&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/mutual-funds/profile/ticker\&#34;>Admiral™ Shares&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;mutual fund.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_earnings_growth_rate&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_earnings_growth_rate&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_earnings_growth_rate&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The average annual rate of growth in earnings over the past five years for the stocks in a portfolio.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vtabx&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vtabx&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vtabx&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Investors should be mindful in evaluating the Vanguard Total International Bond Index Fund Admiral Shares current SEC yield. This yield, while accurately calculated based on the SEC requirements, does not capture returns resulting from currency hedging. This fund includes bonds that are denominated in local currencies and hedges returns back to the U.S. dollar to minimize currency risk. Currency hedging can have a meaningful impact on total returns over the short term.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_expense_ratio_fund_ids&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_expense_ratio_fund_ids&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_expense_ratio_fund_ids&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>0869,0869,1860,0856,3184,0884,0513,0223,0920,0239,0964,1865,0923,0085,0530,4430,4415,V014,V038,2020,4438,0967,0961,0932,0939,0935,0938,0969,0937,0966,0868,0807,0864,0866,0857,0865,0867,1859,1861,0504,0545,0732,1874,1872,0733,1646,1647,1645,3138,3139,3137,0838,0839,0828,3348,3350,3349,3351,3353,3352,3354,1848,1850,1849,1851,1853,1852,1854,0103,5102,0116,0135,0118,1643,1644,1642,V042,1948,1648,1867,2011,0723,0724,0914,0122,0122&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_mf_non_vg_net_expense_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_mf_non_vg_net_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_mf_non_vg_net_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A fund&#39;s annual operating expenses expressed as a percentage of average net assets, reflecting fee waivers or expense reimbursements made to investors by the fund. The expense ratio is calculated annually and includes management fees, administrative fees, and any marketing and distribution fees. It doesn&#39;t include loads or purchase or redemption fees, if any.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Non-Vanguard fund expense ratio data provided by Morningstar are for the fund&#39;s latest fiscal year and may vary from current expense ratios. For more complete information about fees and expenses, see the fee table in the fund&#39;s prospectus. Vanguard is not responsible for the accuracy or timeliness of third-party data.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_sector_specialityfilter&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/configuration/configuration_sector_specialityfilter&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_sector_specialityfilter&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>[&#39;VASFX&#39;,&#39;VMNIX&#39;,&#39;VMNFX&#39;]&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_morningstar_all_rights_reserved&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_morningstar_all_rights_reserved&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_morningstar_all_rights_reserved&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>© 2025 Morningstar, Inc. All Rights Reserved. The information contained herein: (1) is proprietary to Morningstar; (2) may not be copied or distributed; and (3) is not warranted to be accurate, complete or timely. Neither Morningstar nor its content providers are responsible for any damages or losses arising from any use of this information. Past performance is no guarantee of future results.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_r_squared_and_beta&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/footnote_r_squared_and_beta&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;footnote_r_squared_and_beta&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>R-squared and beta are calculated from trailing 36-month fund returns relative to the associated benchmark.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_non_vg_fund_not_available&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_non_vg_fund_not_available&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_non_vg_fund_not_available&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>This fund is not available for purchase or transfer&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>This fund is not available for purchase and cannot be transferred to your Vanguard Brokerage Services® account from another financial institution. Contact Vanguard Brokerage Services at 800-992-8327 for more information.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_average_stated_maturity&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_average_stated_maturity&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_average_stated_maturity&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Average Stated Maturity represents the average of the stated maturity dates for all fixed income securities held by the fund.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The longer the average maturity, the more a fund&#39;s share price will move up or down in response to changes in interest rates.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_also_available_links_lower_admiral&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_also_available_links_lower_admiral&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_also_available_links_lower_admiral&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Also available at a lower cost as an&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/mutual-funds/profile/ticker\&#34;>Admiral™ Shares&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;mutual fund.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_past_performance_mutualfund&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_past_performance_mutualfund&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_past_performance_mutualfund&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>The performance data shown represent past performance, which is not a guarantee of future results. Investment returns and principal value will fluctuate so that investors&#39; shares, when sold, may be worth more or less than their original cost. Current performance may be lower or higher than the performance data cited.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;i>Performance data for periods of less than one year does not reflect the deduction of purchase and redemption fees. Maintenance, low balance, and service fees may be assessed by some funds. None of these fees are reflected in the performance figures. If these fees were included, the performance would be lower. All other performance data are adjusted for purchase and redemption fees, where applicable.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;i>Performance data do not reflect the deduction of the $25 annual account service fee that may be applied to certain accounts. If this fee was included, performance would be lower.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_portfolio_composition_file_authorized_participant&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_portfolio_composition_file_authorized_participant&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_portfolio_composition_file_authorized_participant&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The Portfolio Composition File identifies the expected name and amount of each security that &amp;quot;authorized participants&amp;quot; were required to deposit/receive with Vanguard to purchase/redeem a Creation Unit of ETF Shares on that date. Except in certain circumstances as deemed appropriate by Vanguard in accordance with applicable internal policies and regulatory requirements, an authorized participant purchasing/redeeming ETF Shares on that date would deposit/receive the same securities in the same amounts as shown on the PCF.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_investing_is_subject_to_risk&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_investing_is_subject_to_risk&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_investing_is_subject_to_risk&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>All investing is subject to risk, including the possible loss of the money you invest. There is no guarantee that any particular asset allocation or mix of funds will meet your investment objectives or provide you with a given level of income. Diversification does not ensure a profit or protect against a loss.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_minimum_tax&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_alternative_minimum_tax&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_minimum_tax&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A separate tax system designed to ensure that wealthy individuals and organizations pay at least a minimum amount of federal income taxes. Certain securities used to fund private, for-profit activities are subject to the AMT.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_abbreviations_for_securities_exchanges&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_abbreviations_for_securities_exchanges&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;Abbreviations for Securities Exchanges&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;table class=\&#34;compare-funds-exchanges\&#34;>\n&lt;thead>&lt;tr>&lt;th>Abbreviation&lt;\/th>\n&lt;th>Exchange Name&lt;\/th>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;\/thead>&lt;tbody>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>A or AOE&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>American Options Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>BATS&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Better Alternative Trading System&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>B or BOX&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Boston Options Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>BOS or BSE&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Boston Stock Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>CIN&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Cincinnati Stock Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>MID&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Chicago Stock Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>NAS&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Nasdaq&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>NYSE&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>New York Stock Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>OBB&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Nasdaq Bulletin Board Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>OTC&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Over the Counter&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>P or PAO&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Pacific Options Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>PHO&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Philadelphia Options Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>PSE&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Pacific Stock Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>W or WCB&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Chicago Board of Options Exchange (CBOE)&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>X or XPH&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>Philadelphia Stock Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;tr>&lt;td>&lt;p>&lt;b>Y or ISO&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;td>&lt;p>International Securities Exchange&lt;\/p>\n&lt;\/td>\n&lt;\/tr>&lt;\/tbody>&lt;\/table>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_portfolio_composition_institutional_investors&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_portfolio_composition_institutional_investors&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_portfolio_composition_institutional_investors&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Institutional investors authorized to create Vanguard ETF® shares for the marketplace were required to deposit the following securities with Vanguard to purchase a creation unit of this ETF fund on the date specified. An authorized participant redeeming shared of this ETF fund on the same date would receive the same securities in the amounts shown.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_important_fund_performance_information&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_important_fund_performance_information&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;a href=\&#34;/content/retail/public/us/en/investor-resources-education/portfolio-management/performance-details.html\&#34;>Important fund performance information&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_non_vanguard_mf_data_sources&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_non_vanguard_mf_data_sources&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Fund price provided by Refinitiv. Disclaimer. Additional data on this page provided by Morningstar®. Disclaimer.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_all_in_one&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_all_in_one&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_all_in_one&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>All-in-one Vanguard funds help simplify the way you manage your portfolio by reducing risk through broad diversification and automatic rebalancing.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_whats_a_management_style&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_whats_a_management_style&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_whats_a_management_style&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Management style is the method used to select a fund&#39;s investments. Indexing seeks to match, rather than outperform, the return and risk characteristics of an index, by holding all, or a representative sample of, the securities that make up the index. Active management seeks to outperform the average returns of the financial market. Active managers rely on research, market forecasts, and their own judgment and experience in selecting securities to buy and sell.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_expense_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/footnote_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;footnote_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Excluding borrowing and dividend expenses on securities sold short, the Total Annual Fund Operating Expenses are 0.25%.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_foreign_exchange&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_foreign_exchange&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_foreign_exchange&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>\u2022 Seeks to capture carry premium in the form of interest rate spreads in currencies.&lt;br>\n\u2022 Holds long positions in higher yielding foreign currencies, while taking short positions in lower yielding foreign currencies.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_load&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_load&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;Load Fund&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Load funds are funds that charge sales fees (or commissions) to purchase or sell shares. Examples of these fees include:&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>\u2022&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Front-end load to purchase shares&lt;\/b>: This fee is deducted from the purchase, which will reduce the amount of money you invest in a fund.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>\u2022&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Contingent deferred sales charge (CDSC)&lt;\/b>, or back-end load, to sell shares: This fee is subtracted from the sale, which will reduce the amount of money you receive from selling an investment.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Note:&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;Vanguard Brokerage Services no longer accepts purchases in funds that charge loads.&amp;nbsp;Vanguard Brokerage Services doesn&#39;t charge additional fees or commissions for the sale of any load fund offered through our FundAccess program. However, the fund family may charge a fee for selling back-end load funds.&lt;br>\nFor more information on Vanguard-specific fees, please see the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/client-benefits/investment-fees\&#34;>&lt;b>Vanguard Brokerage Services commission and fee schedule&lt;\/b>&lt;\/a>.&amp;nbsp;For more information on fund-specific fees, make sure to read the fund prospectus before investing.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_p529_program_description_link1&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_p529_program_description_link1&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_p529_program_description_link1&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;a href=\&#34;https://personal.vanguard.com/us/LiteratureRequest?FW_Activity=FindLiteratureActivity&amp;amp;FW_Event=specialnotice\&#34;>&lt;b>See a special notice to non-U.S. investors.&lt;\/b>&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_p529_program_description_link2&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_p529_program_description_link2&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_p529_program_description_link2&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>For more information about The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan, obtain a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://personal.vanguard.com/pdf/529progdesc.pdf?cbdForceDomain=true\&#34;>&lt;b>Program Description(PDF)&lt;\/b>&lt;\/a>, which includes investment objectives, risks, charges, expenses, and other information; read and consider it carefully before investing. Vanguard Marketing Corporation, Distributor.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_bndx&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_bndx&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_bndx&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Investors should be mindful in evaluating the Vanguard Total International Bond ETF current SEC yield. This yield, while accurately calculated based on the SEC requirements, does not capture returns resulting from currency hedging. This fund includes bonds that are denominated in local currencies and hedges returns back to the U.S. dollar to minimize currency risk. Currency hedging can have a meaningful impact on total returns over the short term.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_etf_performance_share_class&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_etf_performance_share_class&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_etf_performance_share_class&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard ETFs® (exchange-traded funds) are a class of shares listed for trading on an exchange. The shares are available only through a broker, including Vanguard Brokerage Services®. The market price is determined by the midpoint between the bid and ask prices as of the closing time of the New York Stock Exchange (typically 4 p.m., Eastern time). The net asset value (NAV) is determined as of the closing time of the New York Stock Exchange (typically 4 p.m., Eastern time).&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_note&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_note&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_note&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The Market price is determined by the midpoint between the bid and asked prices as of the closing time of the New York Stock Exchange (typically 4 p.m .,Eastern time) on business days.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_commodities&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_commodities&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_long_short_commodities&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>\u2022 Seeks to capture the risk premium associated with inventory levels in commodities.&lt;br>\n\u2022 Hold long positions in commodity futures expected to increase in price (backwardation), while taking short positions in commodity futures expected decline in price (contango).&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_past_performance_etf&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_past_performance_etf&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_past_performance_etf&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>The performance data shown represent past performance, which is not a guarantee of future results. Investment returns and principal value will fluctuate so that investors&#39; shares, when sold, may be worth more or less than their original cost. Current performance may be lower or higher than the performance data cited.&amp;nbsp;The performance of an index is not an exact representation of any particular investment, as you cannot invest directly in an index.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_average_effective_maturity&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_average_effective_maturity&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_average_effective_maturity&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Average Effective Maturity is defined as the average length of time until fixed income securities held by a fund are expected to be repaid, taking into consideration that an action such as a call or refunding may cause some bonds to be repaid before they mature.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The longer the average maturity, the more a fund&#39;s share price will move up or down in response to changes in interest rates.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_style&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_style&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_style&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>This is a fund&#39;s investing approach for achieving its primary goal.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Value&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;funds are the least volatile of the three styles. They focus on stocks of typically longer-standing companies that use their earnings to pay dividends, not necessarily to reinvest in the company. Potential returns are generated more by dividend income than capital appreciation.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Blend&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;funds buy both value and growth stocks.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Growth&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;funds are the most volatile of the three styles. They focus on stocks of companies that tend to reinvest their earnings into expansion and acquisition efforts to help grow the company. Potential returns are generated more by capital appreciation than by dividend income.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_average_duration&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_average_duration&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_average_duration&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A measure of the sensitivity of bond\u2014and bond mutual fund\u2014prices to interest rate movements. For example, if a bond has a duration of 2 years, its price would fall about 2% when interest rates rose 1 percentage point. On the other hand, the bond&#39;s price would rise by about 2% when interest rates fell by 1 percentage point.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_what_are_share_classes&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_what_are_share_classes&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_what_are_share_classes&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A mutual fund may offer more than one &amp;quot;class&amp;quot; of shares to investors. Each class represents a similar interest in the mutual fund&#39;s portfolio, but is offered at a different price. Fees and expenses will vary according to class; therefore, investment returns will differ.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Investor Shares&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;offer the lowest minimum investment amounts.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Admiral&lt;sup>TM&lt;\/sup>&amp;nbsp;Shares&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;have higher investment minimums but lower expense ratios.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Institutional Shares&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;are available to institutional investors. These have much higher minimum investments and are not available to retail investors.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_price&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_price&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_price&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>For ETFS, the market price is determined by the midpoint between the bid and ask prices as of the closing time of the New York Stock Exchange (typically 4 p.m., Eastern time) on business days. Daily mutual fund NAVs are displayed on our website between 6 p.m. and 8 p.m., Eastern time. NAVs displayed prior to 8:00 p.m., Eastern time are preliminary and subject to change.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_payable_date&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_payable_date&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_payable_date&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The date when dividends or capital gains are paid to shareholders. For Vanguard mutual funds, the payable date is usually within 2 to 4 days of the record date. The payable date also refers to the date on which a declared stock dividend or bond interest payment is scheduled to be paid.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_529_college_savings_plan&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_529_college_savings_plan&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_529_college_savings_plan&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&amp;lt;i&amp;gt;For more information about The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan, obtain a&amp;amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;a href=&amp;quot;https://personal.vanguard.com/pdf/529progdesc.pdf?cbdForceDomain=true&amp;quot; target=&amp;quot;_blank&amp;quot;&amp;gt;Program Description (PDF)&amp;lt;i&amp;nbsp; class=&amp;quot;fa fa-file-pdf-o&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;, which includes investment objectives, risks, charges, expenses, and other information; read and consider it carefully before investing. Vanguard Marketing Corporation, Distributor.&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_whats_an_investment_minimum&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_whats_an_investment_minimum&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_whats_an_investment_minimum&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;We make a range of investment minimums available to meet the needs of all investors.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;Mutual funds &amp;amp; 529s&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;Minimum initial investments aren&#39;t based on the fund&#39;s share price. Instead, they&#39;re a flat dollar amount.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;ETFs&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;You can buy a Vanguard exchange-traded fund (ETF) for as little as $1, regardless of the ETF\u2019s share price.&amp;nbsp; Fractional shares are only available when buying a Vanguard ETF.&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_daily_net_shareholder_cash_flow&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_daily_net_shareholder_cash_flow&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_daily_net_shareholder_cash_flow&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The amount of money that flows into or out of a mutual fund on a given day. This is calculated by subtracting a fund&#39;s redemptions from its purchases.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_alternative_minimum_tax&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/footnote_alternative_minimum_tax&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;footnote_alternative_minimum_tax&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Alternative minimum tax (AMT) percentage represents the fund&#39;s income subject to the AMT as of the date indicated.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_why_should_i_care_about_risk&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_why_should_i_care_about_risk&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_why_should_I_care_about_risk&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Risk is a measure of how likely it is that you could lose money in an investment. Knowing the risk level you&#39;re comfortable with and the length of time you expect to invest can help you select an appropriate fund for your investing needs.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definition_529_portoflio_advisor_structure&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definition_529_portoflio_advisor_structure&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definition_529_portoflio_advisor_structure&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;The portfolio does not employ an investment\nadvisor, but it benefits from the investment\nadvisory services of the underlying Vanguard\nmutual fund(s) in which it invests.&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_mf_tax_exempt_money_market_lose_money&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_mf_tax_exempt_money_market_lose_money&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_mf_tax_exempt_money_market_lose_money&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard Cash Reserves Federal Money Market Fund and Vanguard Federal Money Market Fund:&lt;i> You could lose money by investing in the Fund. Although the Fund seeks to preserve the value of your investment at $1.00 per share, it cannot guarantee it will do so. An investment in the Fund is not a bank account and is not insured or guaranteed by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or any other government agency. The Fund\u2019s sponsor is not required to reimburse the Fund for losses, and you should not expect that the sponsor will provide financial support to the Fund at any time, including during periods of market stress.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_non_vanguard_third_party_price_calculations&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_non_vanguard_third_party_price_calculations&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Fund prices are provided or calculated using data from third-party sources. Vanguard is not responsible for the accuracy or timeliness of third-party data.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_government&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_government&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_government&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Government money market funds are open to all investors, and seek to maintain a stable $1 net asset value. They&#39;re exempt from liquidity fees and redemption gates, but can adopt them voluntarily if previously disclosed to investors. Vanguard has chosen not to subject the fund to liquidity fees or redemption gates.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;br>\nThese funds must hold at least 99.5% of assets in cash, U.S. government securities, and/or repurchase agreements that are collateralized solely by U.S. government securities or cash.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_individual_balanced_portfolios&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_individual_balanced_portfolios&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_individual_balanced_portfolios&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Are multi-asset class portfolios that maintain a diversified allocation to various asset classes.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_fixed_income&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_fixed_income&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_fixed_income&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>\u2022 Seeks to exploit the steepness in the treasury yield curve created by investors\u2019 desire to hold the short end of the curve.&lt;br>\n\u2022 Holds long positions in treasury futures diversified across multiple points on the yield curve.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_past_performance_529&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_past_performance_529&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_past_performance_529&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>The performance data shown represent past performance, which is not a guarantee of future results. Investment returns and principal value will fluctuate so that investors&#39; units, when sold, may be worth more or less than their original cost. Current performance may be lower or higher than the performance data cited.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_market_capitalization&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_market_capitalization&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_market_capitalization&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>This measures the size of a company by multiplying the number of its outstanding stock shares by the current price of a single share.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;ul>\n&lt;li>&lt;b>&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Large-cap:&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;More than $15.6 billion.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>&lt;b>&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Mid-cap:&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;$2.1 billion to $15.6 billion.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>&lt;b>&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Small-cap:&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;Less than $2.1 billion.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;\/ul>\n&lt;p>For a fund, this is calculated by taking an average (&amp;quot;median&amp;quot;) of the capitalization of all of the stocks that the fund invests in.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_strategyfilter_esg&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/configuration/configuration_strategyfilter_esg&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_strategyfilter_ESG&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>[&#39;VSGX&#39;, &#39;VCEB&#39;, &#39;ESGV&#39;, &#39;VFTAX&#39;, &#39;VEIGX&#39;, &#39;VESGX&#39;, &#39;VBPIX&#39;, &#39;VEOIX&#39;, &#39;VEOAX&#39;]&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_fund_characteristics_non_vg_fund_tt&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_fund_characteristics_non_vg_fund_tt&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_fund_characteristics_non_vg_fund_tt&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>All investing is subject to risk, including possible loss of principal. There may be other material differences between products that must be considered prior to investing.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>For more information about non-Vanguard funds offered through Vanguard Brokerage Services, visit vanguard.com to obtain a prospectus or, if available, a summary prospectus. Investment objectives, risks, charges, expenses, and other important information&amp;nbsp; are contained in the prospectus; read and consider it carefully before investing.&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;i>Vanguard ETF Shares are not redeemable with the issuing Fund other than in very large aggregations worth millions of dollars. Instead, investors must buy and sell Vanguard ETF Shares in the secondary market and hold those shares in a brokerage account. In doing so, the investor may incur brokerage commissions and may pay more than net asset value when buying and receive less than net asset value when selling.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>© 2024 The Vanguard Group, Inc. All rights reserved.&amp;nbsp; Vanguard Marketing Corporation, Distributor.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_credit_quality&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_credit_quality&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_credit_quality&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>This measures a bond issuer&#39;s ability to repay interest and principal on time. For a fund, it&#39;s calculated by taking an average of the credit ratings for all of the bonds that the fund invests in.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_holding_details&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_holding_details&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_holding_details&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>Disclosing portfolio holdings&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Vanguard may publish on this site, in the fund&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Portfolio &lt;\/b>details, the 10 largest stock portfolio holdings of a Vanguard fund\u2014including the percentage of the fund&#39;s total assets that each of these holdings represents\u2014as of the most recent calendar-quarter-end. This information will generally be published 15 calendar days after the end of the calendar quarter (except for Vanguard index funds, which will generally be published 15 calendar days after the end of the month).&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Vanguard may also publish on this site, in the fund&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Portfolio &lt;\/b>details, the 10 largest stock portfolio holdings of a Vanguard fund\u2014including the aggregate percentage that these holdings represent of the fund&#39;s total net assets\u2014as of the most recent month-end. This information will generally be published 10 business days after the end of the month.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Vanguard may also publish on this site, in the fund&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Portfolio &lt;\/b>details, a detailed list of the securities held in certain actively managed Vanguard ETFs and certain Vanguard index ETFs (portfolio holdings) on a daily basis.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Vanguard may also publish on this site, in the fund&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Portfolio &lt;\/b>details, a detailed list of the securities (aggregated by issuer for money market funds) held in a Vanguard fund (portfolio holdings) as of the most recent calendar-quarter-end. This information would be published 30 days after the end of the calendar quarter, except for:&lt;\/p>\n&lt;ul>\n&lt;li>Vanguard Market Neutral Fund, for which information would be published 60 calendar days after the end of the calendar quarter.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>Vanguard index funds (except for certain Vanguard index ETFs) and Vanguard actively managed fixed income funds, for which information would be published 15 calendar days after the end of the month.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>Vanguard money market funds, for which information would be published within 5 business days after the last business day of the preceding month.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;\/ul>\n&lt;p>Except with respect to Vanguard money market funds:&lt;\/p>\n&lt;ul>\n&lt;li>Vanguard may exclude any portion of these portfolio holdings from publication on this site when deemed in the best interest of the fund.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>The portfolio holdings are provided on a delayed basis and won&#39;t necessarily represent all of the actual investments held by the relevant Vanguard fund.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;\/ul>\n&lt;p>Portfolio holdings may exclude any temporary cash investments and equity index products.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Terms &amp;amp; conditions&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The following additional terms and conditions apply to the publication on this site of any Vanguard fund&#39;s portfolio holdings as described above:&lt;\/p>\n&lt;ul>\n&lt;li>By accessing the portfolio holdings, you agree not to reproduce, distribute, or disseminate the portfolio holdings, in whole or in part, in any form without prior written permission from Vanguard.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>Except with respect to Vanguard money market funds, the portfolio holdings are provided on an &amp;quot;as is&amp;quot; basis. Vanguard makes no express or implied warranties or representations with respect to the accuracy, completeness, reliability, or fitness of the portfolio holdings or any financial results you may achieve from their use.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>In no event shall Vanguard or its affiliates have any liability relating to the use of the portfolio holdings.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;\/ul>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_distribution_yield&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_distribution_yield&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_distribution_yield&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The fund&#39;s current monthly income dividend per share, annualized by dividing by the number of days in the month and multiplying by 365, and shown as a percentage of the fund&#39;s average net asset value (NAV) during the month.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Distribution yields are not available for products with less than 12 months of distribution history.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_closing_market_price&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/price/fund_definitions_closing_market_price&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;Market price&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Represents the ETF\u2019s official closing price as reported by each ETF\u2019s primary exchange.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_iov_ticker_symbol&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_iov_ticker_symbol&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_iov_ticker_symbol&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Intraday optimized value (IOV), also known as the intraday indicative value (IIV), is the calculated per-share price of the ETF, which is published every 15 seconds based on the last sale price of each of the underlying securities in the portfolio basket, plus any estimated cash amounts associated with the creation unit.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_mf_etf_performance_standardized_returns&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_mf_etf_performance_standardized_returns&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_mf_etf_performance_standardized_returns&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>To see quarterly fee-adjusted returns, refer to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Price&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;&amp;amp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Performance&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;details.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_yield&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/price/fund_definitions_yield&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_yield&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A non-money market fund&#39;s SEC yield is based on a formula mandated by the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) that calculates a fund&#39;s hypothetical annualized income as a percentage of its assets.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>A security&#39;s income, for the purposes of this calculation,is based on the current market yield to maturity (for bonds) or projected dividend yield (for stocks) of the fund&#39;s holdings over a trailing 30-day period. This hypothetical income will differ (at times, significantly) from the fund&#39;s actual experience; as a result, income distributions from the fund may be higher or lower than implied by the SEC yield.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The SEC yield for a money market fund is calculated by annualizing its daily income distributions for the previous 7 days.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_mf_etf_performance_expense_ratios&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_mf_etf_performance_expense_ratios&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_mf_etf_performance_expense_ratios&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Expense ratios are displayed on&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Overview.&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;For investments that are less than 1 fiscal year old, expense ratios are estimated.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vaipx&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vaipx&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vaipx&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The yield quoted is the real yield, or the yield before adjusting for inflation. The actual yield of Vanguard Inflation-Protected Securities Fund will be a combination of the real yield and an inflation adjustment. A complete estimate of the fund&#39;s yield requires that an estimate of future inflation be added to the real yield. Because inflation fluctuates, it cannot be projected into the future precisely enough to be included in the yield quote. The inflation adjustment is based on changes to the Consumer Price Index (CPI) and can be either positive or negative, based on the change to the CPI. Investors interested in maintaining the purchasing power of their investment should invest their dividend distributions.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_municipal_money_market&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_municipal_money_market&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_municipal_money_market&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard&#39;s Municipal Money Market Funds:&lt;i>&lt;br>\n The Fund is only available to retail investors (natural persons). You could lose money by investing in the Fund. Although the Fund seeks to preserve the value of your investment at $1.00 per share, it cannot guarantee it will do so. The Fund may impose a fee upon the sale of your shares. An investment in the Fund is not a bank account and is not insured or guaranteed by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or any other government agency. The Fund\u2019s sponsor is not required to reimburse the Fund for losses, and you should not expect that the sponsor will provide financial support to the Fund at any time, including during periods of market stress.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_merger_arbitrage&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_merger_arbitrage&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_alternative_strategies_merger_arbitrage&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>\u2022 Seeks to capture the risk premium associated with M&amp;amp;A deal failure risk.&lt;br>\n\u2022 Holds long positions in the stocks of companies being acquired and may take short positions in the stocks of the acquiring companies.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_delayedprice-1&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_delayedprice-1&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_delayedprice&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Quotes delayed at least 15 minutes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;i>Source:&lt;\/i>&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=\&#34;primary-reinforce\&#34; href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/external-site-message?url=http://www.factset.com/\&#34; title=\&#34;Follow link\&#34;>&lt;b>FactSet&lt;\/b>&lt;\/a>&lt;i>.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_important_etf_information&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_important_etf_information&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/list/etfs\&#34;>Important Vanguard ETF performance information&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_hard_closed_to_all_investors&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_hard_closed_to_all_investors&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_hard_closed_to_all_investors&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Closed to all investors.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_non_vanguard_mf_fees_and_minimums&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_non_vanguard_mf_fees_and_minimums&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>NTF, TF, and load funds are subject to the greater of the FundAccess minimum investment requirements or those identified in the fund&#39;s prospectus. Vanguard Brokerage Services may negotiate fund minimum investment requirements that are greater than or less than the program standards noted above. Individual fund families and funds may impose additional fees, such as purchase fees, redemption fees, 12b-1 fees or other charges. All transactions are subject to any applicable terms and conditions in a Fund&#39;s prospectus, including, but not limited to, any applicable fees or other frequent trading and market-timing policies and procedures imposed by the Fund. For complete information, read the prospectus carefully before investing. The offering conditions of the various funds included in the FundAccess program are subject to change at any time, including, but not limited to, fee classification (load, TF, or NTF) and transfer eligibility. All transactions are also subject to Vanguard Brokerage Services&#39; commission and fee schedules, policies, and procedures.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vtip&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vtip&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vtip&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The yield quoted is the real yield, or the yield before adjusting for inflation. The actual yield on Vanguard Short-Term Inflation-Protected Securities Fund will be a combination of the real yield and an inflation adjustment. A complete estimate of the funds yield requires that an estimate of future inflation be added to the real yield. Because inflation fluctuates, it cannot be projected into the future precisely enough to be included in the yield quote. The inflation adjustment is based on changes to the Consumer Price Index (CPI) and can either be positive or negative, based on the change to the CPI. Investors interested in maintaining the purchasing power of their investment should reinvest their dividend distributions.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_also_available_links_investors&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_also_available_links_investors&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_also_available_links_investors&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Also available at a lower minimum as an&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/mutual-funds/profile/ticker\&#34;>Investor Shares&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;mutual fund.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_also_available_links_investors_mutual_funds&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_also_available_links_investors_mutual_funds&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_also_available_links_investors_mutual_funds&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Also available as an &lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/mutual-funds/profile/ticker\&#34;>Investor Shares&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;mutual fund&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_avg_expense_ratio_similar_funds&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/footnote_avg_expense_ratio_similar_funds&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;footnote_avg_expense_ratio_similar_funds&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Most recent data available. © 2025 Morningstar, Inc. All rights reserved. The information contained herein: (1) is proprietary to Morningstar and/or its content providers; (2) may not be copied or distributed; (3) does not constitute investment advice offered by Morningstar; and (4) is not warranted to be accurate, complete, or timely. Neither Morningstar nor its content providers are responsible for any damages or losses arising from any use of this information. Past performance is no guarantee of future results.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_risk_ratings&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_risk_ratings&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_risk_ratings&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>An investment in the fund could lose money over short or even long periods. You should expect the fund\u2019s share price and total return to fluctuate within a wide range, like the fluctuations of the overall stock market.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_also_available_links_etf_and_lower_admiral&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_also_available_links_etf_and_lower_admiral&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_also_available_links_etf_and_lower_admiral&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Also available as an &lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/etfs/profile/tickerETF\&#34;>ETF&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;(starting at the price of one share) and at a lower cost as an &lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/investment-products/mutual-funds/profile/tickerAdmiral\&#34;>Admiral™ Shares&lt;\/a> mutual fund.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_3&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_risk_scale_3&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_3&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard funds classified as moderate are subject to a moderate degree of fluctuation in share prices. In general, such funds may be appropriate for investors who have a relatively long-term investment horizon (more than 5 years).&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_etf_performance_prospectuses&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_etf_performance_prospectuses&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_etf_performance_prospectuses&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>For more information about Vanguard ETFs, visit vanguard.com to obtain a prospectus or, if available, a summary prospectus. Investment objectives, risks, charges, expenses, and other important information about a fund are contained in the prospectus; read and consider it carefully before investing.&lt;br>\n&lt;br>\n&lt;i>Vanguard ETF Shares are not redeemable with the issuing Fund other than in very large aggregations worth millions of dollars. Instead, investors must buy and sell Vanguard ETF Shares in the secondary market and hold those shares in a brokerage account. In doing so, the investor may incur brokerage commissions and may pay more than net asset value when buying and receive less than net asset value when selling.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_2&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_risk_scale_2&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_2&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard funds classified as conservative to moderate are subject to low to moderate fluctuations in share prices. In general, such funds may be appropriate for investors with medium-term investment horizons (4 to 10 years).&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_1&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_risk_scale_1&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_1&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard funds are classified as conservative if their share prices are expected to remain stable or to fluctuate only slightly. Such funds may be appropriate for the short-term reserves portion of a long-term investment portfolio or for investors with short-term investment horizons (3 years or less).&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vtspx&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vtspx&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vtspx&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The yield quoted is the real yield, or the yield before adjusting for inflation. The actual yield of Vanguard Inflation-Protected Securities Fund will be a combination of the real yield and an inflation adjustment. A complete estimate of the fund&#39;s yield requires that an estimate of future inflation be added to the real yield. Because inflation fluctuates, it cannot be projected into the future precisely enough to be included in the yield quote. The inflation adjustment is based on changes to the Consumer Price Index (CPI) and can be either positive or negative, based on the change to the CPI. Investors interested in maintaining the purchasing power of their investment should invest their dividend distributions.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions__realized_gains_and_losses&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions__realized_gains_and_losses&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_realized_gains_and_losses&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A realized capital gain (or loss) is an increase (or decrease) in the value of a security that is &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; because the security has been sold by the portfolio manager. The capital gains and losses are &amp;quot;realized&amp;quot; by the fund, and any distributions to shareholders as a result of realized gains (adjusted for any realized losses) are taxable during the tax year in which the security was sold.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Realized losses can be used to offset realized gains in an attempt to reduce taxable gains. If realized losses are higher than realized gains, a fund can &amp;quot;carry forward&amp;quot; these excess losses to offset future gains.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_mf_non_vg_gross_expense_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_mf_non_vg_gross_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_mf_non_vg_gross_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>What it costs a fund provider to run a fund. The expense ratio is calculated annually and includes management fees, administrative fees, and any marketing and distribution fees. It doesn&#39;t include loads or purchase or redemption fees, if any.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Non-Vanguard fund gross expense ratio data provided by Morningstar are for the fund&#39;s latest fiscal year and may vary from current gross expense ratios. Such data do not reflect fee waivers or expense reimbursements, which the applicable fund manager may discontinue at any time. For more complete information about fees and expenses, see the fee table in the fund&#39;s prospectus. Vanguard is not responsible for the accuracy or timeliness of third-party data.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_assetclass_risks&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_assetclass_risks&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Target-date investments are subject to the risks of their underlying funds. The year in the investment name refers to the approximate year (the target date) when an investor would retire and leave the workforce. The investment will gradually shift its emphasis from more aggressive investments to more conservative ones based on its target date. A target-date investment is not guaranteed at any time, including on or after the target date.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Bond funds are subject to the risk that an issuer will fail to make payments on time, and that bond prices will decline because of rising interest rates or negative perceptions of an issuer&#39;s ability to make payments.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>U.S. government backing of Treasury or agency securities applies only to the underlying securities and does not prevent share-price fluctuations. Unlike stocks and bonds, U.S. Treasury bills are guaranteed as to the timely payment of principal and interest.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Although the income from a municipal bond fund is exempt from federal tax, you may owe taxes on any capital gains realized through the fund&#39;s trading or through your own redemption of shares. For some investors, a portion of the fund&#39;s income may be subject to state and local taxes, as well as to the federal Alternative Minimum Tax.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>High-yield bonds generally have medium- and lower-range credit quality ratings and are therefore subject to a higher level of credit risk than bonds with higher credit quality ratings.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Derivatives are subject to a number of risks, such as liquidity risk interest rate risk, market risk, credit risk, and management risk.&amp;nbsp; A fund investing in a derivative instrument could lose more than the principal amount invested.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Prices of mid- and small-cap stocks often fluctuate more than those of large-company stocks.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Stocks of companies based in emerging markets are subject to national and regional political and economic risks and to the risk of currency fluctuations. These risks are especially high in emerging markets.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Currency hedging risk is the chance that currency hedging transactions may not perfectly offset a fund&#39;s foreign currency exposures and may eliminate any chance for a fund to benefit from favorable fluctuations in relevant currency exchange rates. Funds incur expenses to hedge currency exposures.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>ESG funds are subject to ESG investment risk, which is the chance that the stocks or bonds screened by the index provider or advisor, as applicable, for ESG criteria generally will underperform the market as a whole or, in the aggregate, will trail returns of other funds screened for ESG criteria. The index provider or advisor\u2019s assessment of a company, based on the company\u2019s level of involvement in a particular industry or their own ESG criteria, may differ from that of other funds or an investor\u2019s assessment of such company. As a result, the companies deemed eligible by the index provider or advisor may not reflect the beliefs and values of any particular investor and may not exhibit positive or favorable ESG characteristics. The evaluation of companies for ESG screening or integration is dependent on the timely and accurate reporting of ESG data by the companies. Successful application of the screens will depend on the index provider or advisor&#39;s proper identification and analysis of ESG data. The advisor may not be successful in assessing and identifying companies that have or will have a positive impact or support a given position. In some circumstances, companies could ultimately have a negative impact or no impact or support a given position.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_5&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_risk_scale_5&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_5&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard funds classified as aggressive are subject to extremely wide fluctuations in share prices. These funds may be appropriate for investors who have a long-term investment horizon (10 years or longer). The unusually high volatility associated with these funds may stem from a number of strategies.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_mutual_fund_redemption_fees&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_mutual_fund_redemption_fees&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>Performance data for periods of less than one year do not reflect the deduction of purchase and redemption fees.&amp;nbsp;Maintenance, low-balance, and service fees may be assessed by some funds. None of these fees are reflected in the performance figures. If these fees were included, the performance would be lower. All other performance data are adjusted for purchase and redemption fees, where applicable.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_4&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_risk_scale_4&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_risk_scale_4&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard funds classified as moderate to aggressive are broadly diversified but are subject to wide fluctuations in share prices because they hold virtually all of their assets in common stocks. These funds may be appropriate for investors who have a long-term investment horizon (10 years or longer).&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_tax_exempt&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_tax_exempt&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_tax_exempt&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>Tax-exempt&lt;br>\n &lt;\/b>Tax-exempt funds seek to provide current income that is exempt from federal personal income taxes. You might consider a tax-exempt fund if:&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>You&#39;re not investing in a tax-advantaged account (these include 401(k)s, IRAs, and 529s).&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>You&#39;re in a higher federal tax bracket (28% or higher).&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/mutual-funds/tax-exempt\&#34;>See if tax-exempt investing is right for you&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_unrealized_gains-_losses&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_unrealized_gains-_losses&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_unrealized_gains_losses&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>An unrealized capital gain (or loss)\u2014also called a &amp;quot;paper profit or loss&amp;quot;\u2014is an increase (or decrease) in the value of a security that isn&#39;t &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; because the security hasn&#39;t been sold.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>When a portfolio manager sells a security, however, the capital gains and losses become &amp;quot;realized&amp;quot; by the fund, and any realized gains (adjusted for any realized losses) are taxable during the tax year in which the security was sold.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Funds with low turnover rates, such as index funds, tend to have more unrealized gains than actively managed funds and are less likely to pass taxable gains on to investors.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>A fund&#39;s unrealized appreciation or depreciation figures are valuable because they can give an idea of whether a fund would need to distribute any gains if all of its securities were sold. Such information may help you determine your potential exposure to taxable distributions.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_delayedprice_factset&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_delayedprice_factset&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_delayedprice_factset&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Quotes delayed at least 15 minutes. Market data provided by FactSet.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_average_maturity&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_average_maturity&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_average_maturity&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Represents the weighted average maturity of the fund&#39;s holdings using the date of the next interest rate adjustment for certain adjustable-rate securities held by the fund. &lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;br>\nThe longer the average maturity, the more a fund&#39;s share price will move up or down in response to changes in interest rates.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_after_tax_returns&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_after_tax_returns&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_after_tax_returns&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>After-tax returns are calculated using the highest individual federal income tax rates in effect at the time of each distribution. They don&#39;t reflect the impact of state and local taxes.&lt;br>\nYou also should know that:&lt;br>\n&lt;br>\n&lt;\/p>\n&lt;ul>\n&lt;li>Your after-tax return depends on your individual tax situation and may differ from the figures presented here.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>If you own a fund in a tax-deferred account, such as an IRA or employer-sponsored retirement plan, this information doesn&#39;t apply to your investment because these accounts aren&#39;t subject to current taxes.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>After-tax returns for Vanguard funds take into account the different tax rates applicable to ordinary income, qualified dividend income, Section 199A dividends, and short-term and long-term capital gains.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>After-tax returns for non-Vanguard funds are provided by Morningstar, Inc., based on data provided by the fund companies. Recent changes in tax law may cause after-tax returns to be calculated inconsistently across different fund families. Accordingly, after-tax returns for peer groups aren&#39;t provided.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>Past performance, whether before or after taxes, doesn&#39;t guarantee future results.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>After-tax returns are quarter-end-adjusted for fees and loads, if applicable.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;\/ul>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>After-tax returns for most funds are calculated using the tax liability implied by each of their respective declared distributions. However, the exact tax characteristics of many distributions aren&#39;t known until after the close of the calendar year.&lt;br>\n&lt;br>\n&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>For Vanguard Tax-Managed Balanced Fund, Vanguard REIT Index Fund, and Vanguard REIT ETF, conservative estimates are used based on fund history until final amounts become available.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_weighted_exposures_chart&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_weighted_exposures_chart&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_weighted_exposures_chart&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Weighted equity exposures exclude any temporary cash investments and equity index futures. Some short-term fixed income securities are classified as cash and are excluded from the weighted bond exposures.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;etf-vanguard-average-expense-ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/etf-vanguard-average-expense-ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_etf_vanguard_average_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard average ETF expense ratio: 0.04%. Industry average ETF expense ratio: 0.23%. All averages are asset-weighted. Industry average excludes Vanguard. Sources: Vanguard and Morningstar, Inc., as of December 31, 2025.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_529_informational_link&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_529_informational_link&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_529_informational_link&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>For more than 20 years, our low-cost funds and expert portfolio management have helped clients save for their loved ones&#39; educational goals.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/accounts-plans/529-plans\&#34;>&lt;b>Learn more about our 529 Plans&lt;\/b>&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_unit_price&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_unit_price&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_unit_price&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Commonly known as net asset value (NAV), a portfolio&#39;s unit price is determined by the value of the portfolio&#39;s total assets, minus liabilities and fees, divided by the number of units outstanding. The value is calculated and displayed at the end of the trading day.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_mf_investing_subject_to_risk&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_mf_investing_subject_to_risk&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_mf_investing_subject_to_risk&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>Total returns:&lt;\/b> Short-term total return information is provided only as a service. Historical performance\u2014particularly short-term performance\u2014is no guarantee of future returns. Price, yield, and return on an actual investment will fluctuate, and you may have a gain or loss when you sell. Average annual returns include changes in price and reinvestments of dividends and capital gains. Since-inception returns for less than 1 year and year-to-date returns aren&#39;t annualized. Index performance is provided as a benchmark but isn&#39;t illustrative of any particular investment. You can&#39;t invest in an index.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Standardized returns:&lt;\/b> To see quarterly fee-adjusted returns, refer to the &lt;b>Price &amp;amp; Performance&lt;\/b> details.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Expense ratios:&lt;\/b> Expense ratios are displayed on &lt;b>Overview&lt;\/b>. For investments that are less than 1 fiscal year old, expense ratios are estimated.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&lt;b>Risk:&lt;\/b> All investing is subject to risk, including the possible loss of the money you invest. Funds that concentrate on a relatively narrow market sector face the risk of higher share-price volatility. Investments in stocks or bonds issued by non-U.S. companies are subject to risks including country/regional risk and currency risk.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_funds_capital_gains_losses&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_funds_capital_gains_losses&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_funds_capital_gains_losses&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;h2>&lt;b>How your fund can affect your taxes&lt;\/b>&lt;\/h2>\n&lt;p>A fund&#39;s capital gains and losses can reveal the tax implications of holding a particular fund&lt;br>\nin a taxable account. This is true of both realized and unrealized capital gains and losses.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_non_vanguard_sec_yield&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/footnote_non_vanguard_sec_yield&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;footnote_non_vanguard_sec_yield&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>For non-Vanguard funds, yield is defined as a fund&#39;s annualized current rate of investment income, calculated with a Securities and Exchange Commission formula that includes the fund&#39;s net income (based on the yield to maturity of each bond it holds), the average number of outstanding fund shares during the 30-day period reported by Morningstar, and the maximum offering price per share on the last day of the period. The data is provided by Morningstar and is only as current as the information supplied to Morningstar by third parties. The yield for a money market fund more closely reflects the current earnings of the fund than its total return.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_individual_portfolios&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_individual_portfolios&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_individual_portfolios&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Are allocated to a single stock, bond, or cash asset class.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_comparison_of_funds&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_comparison_of_funds&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_comparison_of_funds&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Only Mutual Funds and ETFs can be compared.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_expense_ratio_announcements&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_expense_ratio_announcements&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_expense_ratio_announcements&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>We just lowered expense ratios for 84 share classes across 53 funds, including this one! &lt;a href=\&#34;https://corporate.vanguard.com/content/corporatesite/us/en/corp/articles/vanguard-delivers-landmark-cost-savings.html\&#34; title=\&#34;https://corporate.vanguard.com/content/corporatesite/us/en/corp/articles/vanguard-delivers-landmark-cost-savings.html\&#34;>Learn more&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_mf_vanguard_average_expense_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_mf_vanguard_average_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_mf_vanguard_average_expense_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard average mutual fund expense ratio: 0.08%. Industry average mutual fund expense ratio: 0.50%. All averages are asset-weighted. Industry average excludes Vanguard. Sources: Vanguard and Morningstar, Inc., as of December 31, 2025.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_terms_and_conditions_portfolio_composition_file&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_terms_and_conditions_portfolio_composition_file&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_terms_and_conditions_portfolio_composition_file&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>By accessing the PCF, you agree not to reproduce, distribute, or disseminate the PCF, in whole or in part, in any form without prior written permission of The Vanguard Group, Inc, (Vanguard) and Morgan Stanley Capital International (MSCI), or any other applicable benchmark provider (Provider). All information in the PCF is provided on an &amp;quot;as is&amp;quot; basis, and Vanguard, MSCI, and Provider make no express or implied warranties or representations of any kind with respect to any of the information contained in the PCF (including, without limitation, with respect to the accuracy, completeness, reliability, merchantability, or fitness for a particular purpose of any such information, or any financial results you may achieve from its use). In no event shall Vanguard, MSCI, Provider, or their respective affiliates have any liability relating to the use of the PCF. The PCF is provided on a delayed basis and does not necessarily represent the holdings of the relevant Vanguard fund, either on the date it was originally published or currently. The PCF is for informational purposes only. You may use the PCF solely in connection with evaluating purchases and sales of Vanguard ETFs®, and may not use it in connection with any other financial product or index.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_target_enrollment_portfolios&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_target_enrollment_portfolios&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_target_enrollment_portfolios&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Are diversified multi-asset class portfolios that automatically adjust asset mix over time, becoming more conservative as you approach the target enrollment year for college.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_tax_managed&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_tax_managed&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_tax_managed&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>Tax-managed&lt;\/b>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Tax-managed funds aim to minimize the impact of taxes on investors&#39; total returns. They&#39;re specifically managed to:&lt;br>\n&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Minimize portfolio turnover.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Minimize capital gains when selling shares.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Avoid securities that provide taxable dividend income.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_529_performance_expense_ratios&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_529_performance_expense_ratios&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_529_performance_expense_ratios&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Expenses for multiple-fund portfolios represent a weighted average of the expenses of the portfolio&#39;s underlying funds. The fees and expenses of the underlying funds may change.&lt;br>\n&lt;br>\nExpense ratios are displayed on a 529 portfolio&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;b>Overview&lt;\/b>. For portfolios that are less than 1 fiscal year old, expense ratios are estimated.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_vanguard_cash_reserves&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_vanguard_cash_reserves&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_vanguard_cash_reserves&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard Cash Reserves Federal Money Market Fund and Vanguard Federal Money Market Fund:&amp;nbsp;&lt;i>You could lose money by investing in the Fund. Although the Fund seeks to preserve the value of your investment at $1.00 per share, it cannot guarantee it will do so. An investment in the Fund is not a bank account and is not insured or guaranteed by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or any other government agency. The Fund\u2019s sponsor is not required to reimburse the Fund for losses, and you should not expect that the sponsor will provide financial support to the Fund at any time, including during periods of market stress.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_money_market_holding_terms_and_conditions&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_money_market_holding_terms_and_conditions&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_money_market_holding_terms_and_conditions&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Please read and indicate your acceptance of these Additional Terms by clicking on the link at the bottom of the page. You are about to enter into an Agreement with CUSIP Global Services. If you do not agree with these terms, then please do not click &amp;quot;I Accept.,&amp;quot;. By clicking &amp;quot;I Accept.,&amp;quot;, you agree to accept and be bound by the terms and conditions of this Agreement.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The CUSIP Data contained in&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;http://www.vanguard.com/\&#34;>vanguard.com&lt;\/a>,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://personal.vanguard.com/us/home\&#34;>personal.vanguard.com&lt;\/a>,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://advisors.vanguard.com/advisors-home\&#34;>advisors.vanguard.com&lt;\/a>, and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://institutional.vanguard.com/VGApp/iip/site/institutional/home\&#34;>institutional.vanguard.com&lt;\/a>&amp;nbsp;(the &amp;quot;Vanguard Web Site&amp;quot;) consists of security identifiers and related descriptive information (&amp;quot;the CUSIP Database&amp;quot;) and is protected under the U.S. copyright laws and is licensed with permission from CUSIP Global Services (&amp;quot;CGS&amp;quot;), on behalf of the American Bankers Association &amp;quot;ABA&amp;quot;.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Visitor agrees and acknowledges that the CUSIP Database and the information contained therein is and shall remain valuable intellectual property owned by, or licensed to, CUSIP Global Services and the American Bankers Association (&amp;quot;ABA&amp;quot;), and that no proprietary rights are being transferred to visitor in such materials or in any of the information contained therein. Any use of the CUSIP Data by visitor outside of the clearing and settlement of transactions requires a license from CGS, along with an associated fee based on usage. Visitor agrees that misappropriation or misuse of such materials will cause serious damage to CGS and ABA, and that in such event money damages may not constitute sufficient compensation to CGS and ABA; consequently, visitor agrees that in the event of any misappropriation or misuse, CGS and ABA shall have the right to obtain injunctive relief in addition to any other legal or financial remedies to which CGS and ABA may be entitled.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Visitor agrees that it shall not publish nor distribute in any medium the CUSIP Database or any substantial portion of the information contained therein or summaries or subsets thereof to any person or entity. Visitor may not create or maintain a master file or database of CUSIP identifiers or descriptions for itself or any third party recipient that is intended to serve as a substitute for any CUSIP service.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Visitor agrees not to:&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Violate the restrictions in any robot inclusion headers on the Vanguard Web Site or in any way bypass or circumvent any other measure employed to limit or prevent access to the CUSIP Data on the Vanguard Web Site;&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Violate the security of the Vanguard Web Site or attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Web Site, CUSIP Data, materials, information, computer systems or networks connected to Vanguard server, through hacking, password mining or any other means; or&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Interfere or attempt to interfere with the proper working of the Vanguard Web Site or any activities conducted on or through the Vanguard Web Site.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>NEITHER CGS, ABA NOR ANY OF THEIR AFFILIATES MAKE ANY WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, AS TO THE ACCURACY, ADEQUACY OR COMPLETENESS OF ANY OF THE INFORMATION CONTAINED IN THE CUSIP DATABASE. ALL SUCH MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED TO VISITOR ON AN &amp;quot;AS IS&amp;quot; BASIS, WITHOUT ANY WARRANTIES AS TO MERCHANTABILITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE OR USE NOR WITH RESPECT TO THE RESULTS WHICH MAY BE OBTAINED FROM THE USE OF SUCH MATERIALS. NEITHER CGS, ABA NOR THEIR AFFILIATES SHALL HAVE ANY RESPONSIBILITY OR LIABILITY FOR ANY ERRORS OR OMISSIONS NOR SHALL THEY BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES, WHETHER DIRECT OR INDIRECT, SPECIAL OR CONSEQUENTIAL, EVEN IF THEY HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE LIABILITY OF CGS, ABA OR ANY OF THEIR AFFILIATES PURSUANT TO ANY CAUSE OF ACTION, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, EXCEED THE FEE PAID BY VISITOR FOR ACCESS TO SUCH MATERIALS IN THE MONTH IN WHICH SUCH CAUSE OF ACTION IS ALLEGED TO HAVE ARISEN. FURTHERMORE, CGS AND ABA SHALL HAVE NO RESPONSIBILITY OR LIABILITY FOR DELAYS OR FAILURES DUE TO CIRCUMSTANCES BEYOND THEIR CONTROL.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Visitor agrees that the foregoing terms and conditions shall survive any termination of its right of access to the materials identified above.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_funds_capital_gains_losses_2&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_funds_capital_gains_losses_2&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_funds_capital_gains_losses_2&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;These tax implications don&#39;t apply to investors holding a fund in a tax-deferred account, such\nas an IRA or employer-sponsored retirement plan.&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_12b1fee&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_12b1fee&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_12b1fee&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>An annual fee charged by some mutual funds to pay for marketing and distribution activities. Like a fund&#39;s expense ratio, the fee is taken directly from fund assets, thus reducing shareholders&#39; total return.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_vipix&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_vipix&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_vipix&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The yield quoted is the real yield, or the yield before adjusting for inflation. The actual yield of Vanguard Inflation-Protected Securities Fund will be a combination of the real yield and an inflation adjustment. A complete estimate of the fund&#39;s yield requires that an estimate of future inflation be added to the real yield. Because inflation fluctuates, it cannot be projected into the future precisely enough to be included in the yield quote. The inflation adjustment is based on changes to the Consumer Price Index (CPI) and can be either positive or negative, based on the change to the CPI. Investors interested in maintaining the purchasing power of their investment should invest their dividend distributions.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_529_performance_not_a_typical_mf_investment&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_529_performance_not_a_typical_mf_investment&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_529_performance_not_a_typical_mf_investment&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan (The Vanguard Plan) is a 529 college savings plan sponsored by the state of Nevada. Although money contributed to The Vanguard Plan will be invested in underlying Vanguard mutual funds, The Vanguard Plan itself isn&#39;t a mutual fund. The State of Nevada has created a trust specifically for the purpose of offering 529 college savings plans, including The Vanguard Plan. An investment in The Vanguard Plan is an investment in municipal fund securities that are issued and offered by the trust. These securities aren&#39;t guaranteed by the State of Nevada, Vanguard, Ascensus Broker Dealer Services, Inc., or any other entity, and aren&#39;t registered with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. Investments in The Vanguard Plan can go up or down in value, and you could lose money by investing in The Vanguard Plan.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;banner_soft_closed_to_new_investors&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/banner/banner_soft_closed_to_new_investors&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;banner_soft_closed_to_new_investors&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Closed to new investors.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_pb_ratio&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_pb_ratio&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_pb_ratio&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The price per share of a stock divided by its book value (i.e., net worth) per share. For a portfolio, the ratio is the weighted average price/book ratio of the stocks it holds.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_acquired_fund_fees_and_expenses&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/footnote/fund_definitions_acquired_fund_fees_and_expenses&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_acquired_fund_fees_and_expenses&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The acquired fund fees and expenses based on the fees and expenses of the underlying funds.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_performance_account_service_fee&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_performance_account_service_fee&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_performance_account_service_fee&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;a href=\&#34;https://investor.vanguard.com/client-benefits/account-fees\&#34;>See Vanguard annual account service fees&lt;\/a>&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;configuration_vanguard_advised_only_icon&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/configuration/configuration_vanguard_advised_only_icon&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;configuration_vanguard_advised_only_icon&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>[&#39;4435&#39;, &#39;4436&#39;, &#39;4437&#39;]&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_effective_maturity_date&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_effective_maturity_date&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_effective_maturity_date&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The length of time until fixed income securities held by a fund reach maturity and are repaid, taking into consideration the possibility that the issuer may call the bond before it&#39;s maturity date.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_reit_yields&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_reit_yields&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Vanguard REIT Index Fund pays quarterly distributions consisting of dividend income, return of capital, and capital gains. However, the tax characteristics of these distributions cannot be determined until after the end of the year since the REITs in which the fund invests do not designate the composition (i.e., dividend income, return of capital, and capital gains) of their payments until the new calendar year.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Since Vanguard cannot know the taxability of the portfolio&#39;s distributions during the year, unadjusted and adjusted effective yields are calculated.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The current unadjusted effective yield is UADJYLDRET_PERCENT as of UADJYLDRET_DATE, which is based on the full amount of REIT distributions (dividend income, as well as return of capital and capital gain).&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>The current adjusted effective yield is ADJYLDREIT_PERCENT as of ADJYLDREIT_DATE. The adjusted yield reflects a reduction in the income included in the yield based on the average return of capital and capital gain distributions received from the fund&#39;s REIT investments for the past 2 calendar years.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>Please remember that the yield is calculated monthly like other stock funds and that Vanguard is not quoting a 30-day SEC yield.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_529_performance_prospectus_information&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_529_performance_prospectus_information&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_529_performance_prospectus_information&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>For more information about The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan, call 866-734-4533 or obtain a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\&#34;https://personal.vanguard.com/pdf/529progdesc.pdf\&#34;>&lt;u>Program Description&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/u>&lt;\/a>PDF, which includes investment objectives, risks, charges, expenses, and other information; read and consider it carefully before investing. Vanguard Marketing Corporation, Distributor and Underwriter. Please note: Before investing in any 529 plan, you should consider whether your or the beneficiary&#39;s home state offers a 529 plan that provides its taxpayers with favorable state tax and other benefits that are only available through investment in the home state&#39;s 529 plan. You also should consult your financial, tax, or other advisor to learn more about how state-based benefits (or any limitations) would apply to your specific circumstances. You also may wish to contact directly your home state&#39;s 529 plan(s), or any other 529 plan, to learn more about those plans&#39; features, benefits, and limitations. Keep in mind that state-based benefits should be one of many appropriately weighted factors to be considered when making an investment decision.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;h5>&lt;b>The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan is a Nevada Trust administered by the Board of Trustees of the College Savings Plans of Nevada, chaired by the Nevada State Treasurer.&lt;\/b>&lt;\/h5>\n&lt;p>The Vanguard Group, Inc., serves as the Investment Manager and through its affiliate, Vanguard Marketing Corporation, markets and distributes the Plan. Ascensus Broker Dealer Services, Inc., serves as Program Manager and has overall responsibility for the day-to-day operations. The Plan\u2019s portfolios, although they invest in Vanguard mutual funds, are not mutual funds. Investment returns are not guaranteed and you could lose money by investing in the Plan.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_tf&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_tf&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_TF&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;b>Transaction-fee (TF) funds&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;are funds that charge fees to trade, such as purchasing, selling, or exchanging shares. These fees apply to each trade you make. Examples of transaction fees include:&lt;\/p>\n&lt;ul>\n&lt;li>&lt;i>&lt;b>Purchase fee&lt;\/b>&lt;\/i>&amp;nbsp;added to your cost of buying shares.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>&lt;b>&lt;i>Sales fee&lt;\/i>&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;subtracted from your proceeds of selling shares.&lt;\/li>\n&lt;li>&lt;b>&lt;i>Exchange fee&lt;\/i>&lt;\/b>&amp;nbsp;paid from your settlement fund. (This fee applies to exchanging shares of a fund for another fund in the same fund family and share class.)&lt;\/li>\n&lt;\/ul>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_mf_etf_529s_performance_total_returns&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_mf_etf_529s_performance_total_returns&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_mf_etf_529s_performance_total_returns&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Short-term total return information is provided only as a service. Historical performance\u2014particularly short-term performance\u2014is no guarantee of future returns. Price, yield, and return on an actual investment will fluctuate, and you may have a gain or loss when you sell. Average annual returns include changes in price and reinvestments of dividends and capital gains. Since-inception returns for less than 1 year and year-to-date returns aren&#39;t annualized. Index performance is provided as a benchmark but isn&#39;t illustrative of any particular investment. You can&#39;t invest in an index.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_beta&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_beta&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_beta&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A measure of the magnitude of a portfolio&#39;s past share-price fluctuations in relation to the ups and downs of the overall market (or appropriate market index). The market (or index) is assigned a beta of 1.00, so a portfolio with a beta of 1.20 would have seen its share price rise or fall by 12% when the overall market rose or fell by 10%. At Vanguard, beta is based on returns over the past 36 months for both the fund and the index.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_reinvest_date&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_reinvest_date&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_reinvest_date&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The date on which an investment&#39;s dividend or capital gains distribution is reinvested, if requested by the shareholder, to purchase additional shares. Also known as the ex-dividend date.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_retail&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_retail&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_retail&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Retail money market funds are limited to individual investors and certain accounts, such as custodial accounts, whose beneficiaries are individuals.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>These funds seek to maintain a stable $1 net asset value. They&#39;re permitted to impose a liquidity fee or a redemption gate if their liquidity falls below regulatory limits.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_detailed_summary_of_the_amendment_tt&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_detailed_summary_of_the_amendment_tt&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_detailed_summary_of_the_amendment_tt&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>&lt;i>The performance data shown represent past performance, which is not a guarantee of future results. Investment returns and principal value will fluctuate, so investors&#39; shares, when sold, may be worth more or less than their original cost. Current performance may be lower or higher than the performance data cited.&lt;\/i>&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>After-tax returns are calculated using the highest individual federal income tax rates in effect at the time of each distribution. They do not reflect the impact of state and local taxes. You also should know that:&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>*Your after-tax return depends on your individual tax situation, and may differ from the figures presented here.&lt;br>\n*If you own fund shares in a tax-deferred account such as an IRA or 401(k) plan, this information does not apply to your investment because these accounts are not subject to current taxes.&lt;br>\n*After-tax returns for Vanguard funds reflect the reduced tax rates on ordinary income, qualified dividend income, and short-term and long-term capital gains that went into effect in 2003.&lt;br>\n*The fund&#39;s past performance-whether before or after taxes-does not guarantee future results.&lt;br>\n*If a fund incurs a loss, which generates a tax benefit, the post-liquidation after-tax return may exceed the fund&#39;s other return figures.&lt;br>\n*After-tax returns are quarter-end adjusted for fees and loads if applicable.&lt;br>\n*After-tax returns for non-Vanguard funds are provided by Morningstar, Inc., based on data provided by the funds. Recent changes in tax law may cause after-tax returns to be calculated inconsistently across different fund families.&lt;\/p>\n&lt;p>After-tax returns for most funds are calculated using the tax liability implied by each fund&#39;s declared distributions. However, the exact tax characteristics of many distributions are not known until after the close of the calendar year.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;fund_definitions_whats_a_strategy&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/fund_definitions/fund_definitions_whats_a_strategy&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;fund_definitions_whats_a_strategy&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>A strategy is the general or specific approach to investing that an individual, institution, or fund manager employs. Choose a strategy based on your goals, risk tolerance, and time horizon.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;disclaimer_p529_program_description&#34;:{&#34;path&#34;:&#34;/content/dam/content-fragments/caas/funds/disclaimer/disclaimer_p529_program_description&#34;,&#34;heading&#34;:&#34;disclaimer_p529_program_description&#34;,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan is a Nevada Trust administered by the office of the Nevada State Treasurer.&lt;br>\nThe Vanguard Group, Inc., serves as the Investment Manager for The Vanguard 529 College Savings Plan and through its affiliate, Vanguard Marketing Corporation, markets and distributes the Plan. Ascensus Broker Dealer Services, LLC, serves as Program Manager and has overall responsibility for the day-to-day operations. The Plan&#39;s portfolios, although they invest in Vanguard mutual funds, are not mutual funds. Investment returns are not guaranteed and you could lose money by investing in the Plan.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;}}'>
    </div>

        <div id="vgn-funds-footnotes-ele" data-vgn-funds-footnotes='{&#34;performance&#34;:{&#34;footnote_market_price&#34;:{&#34;id&#34;:1,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Effective July 15, 2024, the market price returns are calculated using the official closing price as reported by the ETF\u2019s primary exchange. Prior to July 15, 2024, the market price returns were calculated using the midpoint between the bid and ask prices as of the closing time of the New York Stock Exchange (typically 4 p.m., Eastern time). The returns shown do not represent the returns you would receive if you traded shares at other times.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_benchmark&#34;:{&#34;id&#34;:2,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;Bloomberg U.S. 3\u201310 Year Government Float Adjusted Index through December 11, 2017; Bloomberg U.S. Treasury 3\u201310 Year Bond Index thereafter.&#34;},&#34;footnote_avg_expense_ratio_similar_funds&#34;:{&#34;id&#34;:3,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Most recent data available. © 2025 Morningstar, Inc. All rights reserved. The information contained herein: (1) is proprietary to Morningstar and/or its content providers; (2) may not be copied or distributed; (3) does not constitute investment advice offered by Morningstar; and (4) is not warranted to be accurate, complete, or timely. Neither Morningstar nor its content providers are responsible for any damages or losses arising from any use of this information. Past performance is no guarantee of future results.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;},&#34;footnote_r_squared_and_beta&#34;:{&#34;id&#34;:4,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>R-squared and beta are calculated from trailing 36-month fund returns relative to the associated benchmark.&lt;\/p>\n&#34;}},&#34;portfolio&#34;:{&#34;creditQualityFootnote&#34;:{&#34;id&#34;:5,&#34;text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Credit-quality ratings are measured on a scale that generally ranges from AAA (highest) to D (lowest). \u201cNR\u201d is used to classify securities for which a rating is not available. NR securities may include internal money market funds, derivatives, and futures. U.S. Treasury, U.S. agency, and U.S. agency mortgage-backed securities appear under \u201cU.S. Government.\u201d Credit-quality ratings for each issue are either obtained from Bloomberg using ratings derived from Moody\u2019s Investors Service (Moody\u2019s), Fitch Ratings (Fitch), and Standard &amp; Poor\u2019s (S&amp;P), or directly from Moody\u2019s and S&amp;P. Credit-quality ratings obtained from Bloomberg use the following methodologies: When ratings from all three agencies are available, the median rating is used; when ratings from only two of the agencies are available, the lower rating is used; and when one rating is available, that rating is used. Credit-quality ratings obtained directly from Moody\u2019s and S&amp;P use the higher rating for each issue. Exposures are calculated using investment book of record positions, which is based on when transactions occur, not when they settle, which can lead to the appearance of temporary negative cash balances or gross exposures greater than 100%.&lt;\/p>&#34;}}}'>
    </div>
  
